ited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T03:26:50-07:00","id":953081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=952658#post952658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plasm. Because how else are you going to have Ghostbusters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosts use essence.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T04:42:10-07:00","id":953096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=953081#post953081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghosts use essence.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So? Geists/Sin-Eaters don't. (Ghosts came first, and I doubt they wanted two main splats using Essence).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T04:48:37-07:00","id":953097,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't mind Sin Eaters using Essence or Ghosts using Plasm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T07:07:24-07:00","id":953145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=953097#post953097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't mind Sin Eaters using Essence or Ghosts using Plasm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the way I see it, Plasm is nothing more than Ghost Essence flavored with Underworld Hot Sauce.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T07:18:46-07:00","id":953148,"title":"","content":"I'm still sad that Ghosts don't use Plasm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T07:22:56-07:00","id":953150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=953096#post953096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So?</div> </div> </div> </div>So you don't need plasm to be a ghostbuster. (That said, I'd rather ghosts had plasm). But anyway, we're digressing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Other sources of unobtainium might be the localities of portals to the otherworlds. Minerals and metals with strange properties that can be found around the intertices in reality you can get near Infrastructure, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T07:50:52-07:00","id":953171,"title":"","content":"&quot;According to this research, all I need for the new cancer treatment serum is a... fresh jackalope heart. What?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Do you know where I can find 57 grams of Lunargent around here?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T09:19:32-07:00","id":953229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=953096#post953096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So? Geists/Sin-Eaters don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Geists do.<br /> <br /> Plasm is more akin to Corpus; hence ectophagia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T11:27:04-07:00","id":953314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=953171#post953171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cAccording to this research, all I need for the new cancer treatment serum is a... fresh jackalope heart. What?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDo you know where I can find 57 grams of Lunargent around here?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>This guy gets it. Unobtanium's primary reason to be is so serve as a McGuffin. (Ideally, the connection between Breakthrough and Unobtanium is going to resonate a bit better than \u201ccure for cancer\u201d and \u201cthe flesh of a legendary animal\u201d; but if that's what it takes to get the scientist out of his lab and interacting with the world, it's served its purpose.)<br /> <br /> Heck, other possibilities for Unobtanium would be \u201cInfrastructure\u201d (that is, an industrial base that's set up to support the Breakthrough in question; related to the God-Machine at the Storyteller's discretion) or Deep Pockets (where the necessary components aren't really all that unusual, just expensive).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-18-2016, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T12:37:36-07:00","id":953353,"title":"","content":"Revising the purchasing scheme somewhat:<br /> <br /> Breakthroughs still cost Insight to learn; they serve as \u201cpower categories\u201d, collections of related Innovations, but don't do anything other than tell you which Innovations you can buy and what kind of Unobtainium you'll need to fuel them. <br /> <br /> Innovations are learned exactly like Specialties: spend an Experience to unlock one Innovation for one Skill. Instead of granting a bonus die to actions covered by the Innovation, the Innovation lets you spend Unobtanium to access an action you wouldn't otherwise be able to attempt. Instead of having dot ratings, Innovations are \u201crated\u201d based on how much Unobtainium you need to use them. <br /> <br /> Write up each Breakthrough by providing a summary of what kind of Unobtainium it features, and a list of sample Innovations. <br /> <br /> Write up each kind of Unobtainium by providing guidelines as to what sorts of things you have to do to acquire and preserve it. <br /> <br /> Write up each Innovation the same way you'd write up an action for a skill (i.e., what's the dice pool, and what are the results of Dramatic Failure, Failure, Success, and Dramatic Success), plus the Unobtainium cost","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T14:35:23-07:00","id":953426,"title":"","content":"I wonder if we could use the mad scientist of Deadlands as inspiration for Genius 2.0.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T17:50:25-07:00","id":953519,"title":"","content":"This isn't Genius 2.0; it's its own thing. But yes; the way Deadlands' mad scientists acquire \u201cghost rock\u201d (I forget their term for it) and use it in all of their inventions? That was definitely an inspiration for Unobtainium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  Fixed typo 03-19-2024, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T19:13:02-07:00","id":953572,"title":"","content":"So, example time: <hr /><b>Research:</b> Investigate why the conservation of matter is violated<br /> <b>Goal:</b> 25 Clues (or 25 Successes on an Extended Research Action, each roll costing a Clue?)<br /> <b>Breakthrough</b>: Pym Particles<br /> <b>Innovations:</b> Expansion of Matter, Contraction of Matter, Increased Density, Quantum Domain Access<br /> <b>Unobtainium:</b> &quot;Megethomorphic Matter&quot;, or material that has been subject to mass increase or decrease (such as a werewolf's flesh, or an object a mage has shrunken through magic). Each Size of the matter in its &quot;true&quot; state can be refined into 1 unit.<br /> <br /> <b>Innovation</b>: Expansion of matter<br /> Utilizing an infusion of Particles, you can draw in virtual matter to increase a target's effective size for a short time.<br /> <b>Skill:</b> Science<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 unit per use<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Science<br /> <b>Roll Result<br /> Dramatic Failure:</b> Expansion is uncontrolled. Roll the unmodified Dice Pool, but each Size increase also inflicts one point of Lethal Damage.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> Momentary molecular flux, but no noticeable increase in size.<br /> <b>Success:</b> Increase an object or creature's Size by 1 for each Success for a Scene. Recalculate derived traits.<br /> <b>Exception Success:</b> Strength may increase with large enough Size increase at ST option. +1 Strength for every 3 or 5 Size increases seems fair.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Target takes a point of Bashing damage or a Condition to represent the physical and mental strain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-18-2016, 10:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T19:21:30-07:00","id":953578,"title":"","content":"I'd expect an Attribute + Skill dice pool, and there should probably be some additional factors such as how long the Innovation's result lasts. Also, the write-up is a bit lacking in terms of what needs to be done to acquire a unit of Megethomorphic Matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T19:40:52-07:00","id":953590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=953578#post953578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd expect an Attribute + Skill dice pool, and there should probably be some additional factors such as how long the Innovation's result lasts. Also, the write-up is a bit lacking in terms of what needs to be done to acquire a unit of Megethomorphic Matter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I edited it since.<br /> <br /> As for the Dice Roll, what about &quot;passive&quot; effects? Also, it feels kinda odd to tie it to a Skill like a Specialty, since Dice Pools usually involve an Attribute too. I'd probably just drop the Skill tie, since Innovations having a Dice Pool means it's using only one Skill anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T20:54:52-07:00","id":953641,"title":"","content":"<b>Investigating to find a Breakthrough</b><br /> <br /> You don't need a lot of Clues to achieve a Breakthrough. What you <i>do</i> need is for every Clue to be Tagged as \u201cMind-Blowing\u201d, i.e. a Breaking Point trigger. \u201c<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">The character witnesses something traumatic, terrifying, or <b>that rattles his understanding of the world</b>.</span>\u201d* (emphasis mine). A discovery that doesn't threaten the mad scientist's grasp on reality isn't enough to provide the paradigm shift needed for a Breakthrough; and Breaking Points as an integral part of the discovery process is part of why the premise is horrific. <br /> <br /> More thoughts in a bit. <br /> <br /> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:10px\">* <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b>, p.29</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:46:59-07:00","id":955150,"title":"","content":"If you're interested in higher-powered mad scientists in ChroD and don't want to have to take the trouble of updating Genius' mechanics, my remake of Mage is heavily inspired by Genius and has full support for mad scientists. But this is good as a minor template, and I like that it clearly contrasts with my vision of Mages: their horror is they've essentially punched a hole in reality, which is quite different from the kind of horror you're exploring here. Mage vs Sorcerer is a major conflict in MtT, and that could easily be Mage vs Mad Scientist. Sorcerers and these mad scientists work by manipulating existing supernatural forces and natural effects, Mages create their own and force reality into their personal set of square holes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:42:55-07:00","id":955249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=955150#post955150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're interested in higher-powered mad scientists in ChroD and don't want to have to take the trouble of updating Genius' mechanics, my remake of Mage is heavily inspired by Genius and has full support for mad scientists.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I want to hack <b>Mage</b> into a Mad Science game, I'll use the \u201cGifted Science\u201d hack from <b>Mage Chroniclers Guide</b> as the starting point. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=955150#post955150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But this is good as a minor template, and I like that it clearly contrasts with my vision of Mages: their horror is they've essentially punched a hole in reality, which is quite different from the kind of horror you're exploring here. Mage vs Sorcerer is a major conflict in MtT, and that could easily be Mage vs Mad Scientist. Sorcerers and these mad scientists work by manipulating existing supernatural forces and natural effects, Mages create their own and force reality into their personal set of square holes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you like what I've come up with; but I'm not interested in contrasting mad scientists with mages. My intent is to address mad science on its own terms, not as a commentary on another gameline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:56:13-07:00","id":955259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=955249#post955249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I want to hack <b>Mage</b> into a Mad Science game, I'll use the \u201cGifted Science\u201d hack from <b>Mage Chroniclers Guide</b> as the starting point. <br /> <br /> I'm glad you like what I've come up with; but I'm not interested in contrasting mad scientists with mages. My intent is to address mad science on its own terms, not as a commentary on another gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's not really what I'm doing either, and I didn't say you were doing that. I'm just commenting on a thematic and mechanical divide between our respective homebrew mad scientist splats, and mentioning that there's enough of it that they could reasonably coexist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T19:40:53-07:00","id":956087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=953641#post953641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Investigating to find a Breakthrough</b><br /> <br /> You don't need a lot of Clues to achieve a Breakthrough. What you <i>do</i> need is for every Clue to be Tagged as \u201cMind-Blowing\u201d, i.e. a Breaking Point trigger. \u201c<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">The character witnesses something traumatic, terrifying, or <b>that rattles his understanding of the world</b>.</span>\u201d* (emphasis mine). A discovery that doesn't threaten the mad scientist's grasp on reality isn't enough to provide the paradigm shift needed for a Breakthrough; and Breaking Points as an integral part of the discovery process is part of why the premise is horrific.<br /> <br /> More thoughts in a bit.<br /> <br /> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:10px\">* <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b>, p.29</span></div> </div> </div> </div>What happens if a Madboy goes through 'Mind-Blowing' events that don't logically connect, like a spatial phenomenon followed by a cryptid? Do the experiences go into a collective pool, or do experiences gained from certain events get earmarked for certain Breakthroughs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T21:33:00-07:00","id":956145,"title":"","content":"This is the Investigation system from <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b>; the Clues don't randomly appear out of nowhere. They're seeded by the Storyteller, based on the Breakthrough the scientist is investigating. So yeah, if she's investigating two Breakthroughs at once, each Clue is going to be for one Breakthrough or the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T04:55:29-07:00","id":956265,"title":"","content":"I don't hav any useful suggestions, but I'm liking this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T05:28:57-07:00","id":956272,"title":"","content":"Here's my thoughts in a nutshell - you're just remaking another Mage variation by focusing entirely on the scientists. And you're going to run into the same problem as Genius, constantly butting its head against the same themes as Mage, just with a different power set. Just... why? Why focus on just some variation of the obsessive doctor Frankenstein? Why limit yourself in that fasion?<br /> <br /> At minimum, I honestly think that a game of occult science* should be more broad that that. Simply by tapping into the whole archetype from just a single season of Buffy the Vampire Slayer, we have sceintists (who experiment on themselvs!), but you also have your Creations, you have enhanced humans, you have genetically bred hybrids, you have crazy machines that do impossible things, plus we should always have some talking heads / brains in jars. Currently, in the CofD, we have five different games tapping into the idea of occult science - Mage, Promethean, Hunter (a few of the conspiracies), Demon and the new Deviant. These are all scattered around and focusing on one aspect of the whole supernatural science theme. <br /> <br /> If you are really keen on making a game of occult science, I fully believe that the game should combine all these things into one. Really dig into the entire breadth of the thing. You can play as both the crazy guy who made the advanced robot, the robot itself, and the enhanced human assistant / Igor archetype. <br /> <br /> * I think occult sciences sounds a lot better than &quot;mad.&quot; Its been in a few threads that people are uncomfortable with the ableism that the term egenders, so I'm sticking with this instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T10:06:52-07:00","id":956393,"title":"","content":"Uh, I kind of disagree? For one thing, I'm getting the idea that this is more of minor template, low-powered thing. So that right there differentiates them from Mages or Geniuses. <br /> <br /> And the problem with &quot;but mad science also encompasses creations and modified experiments&quot; is that we already have that. We already have Promethean and Deviant. There isn't really a way to have a mad scientist &quot;splat&quot; encompass those without conflicting. Especially a minor template. &quot;Obsessive doctor&quot; is fine for a minor template. Hell, the devs repeatedly describe Mages as &quot;obsessive detectives&quot;- is that too narrow? <br /> <br /> All in all, I don't really see your objections. In particular, I don't think it's a good idea to roll content from five different games into one and expect something coherent. You can establish that these particular mad scientists are connected, put in some hooks that they developed Thaumatech, maybe they make Prometheans semi-regularly...but you can't just roll it all into one ball and have something elegant. Also, sometimes (a lot of the time, actually) a narrower scope can be nice. Again, especially for a minor template.<br /> <br /> I mean, the &quot;too narrow&quot; thing made no sense for Genius. You could experiment on yourself and play a posthuman proto-Deviant. You could create beings using Automata, and those beings could become Inspired- so you could totally play as a mad scientist's creation. You could even play a Mane. So it didn't make sense there. And with this idea, it doesn't make sense for the opposite reason: because it would disrupt the focus of this project.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 08-23-2016, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T12:10:49-07:00","id":956479,"title":"","content":"Honestly, my aim is for \u201cminor template\u201d to be a bit of a stretch; these mad scientists/geniuses/whateveryou want to call them are a \u201cminor template\u201d in the same sense that hunters are a minor template. There's a reason why I chose to title this as \u201cMad <i>Science</i>\u201d instead of \u201cMad <i>Scientist</i>\u201d, and why I described the difference between mortal, hunter, and mad scientist solely in terms of how they react to encountering the supernatural. (Also, I'm not going to back off of \u201cMad\u201d; \u201cMad Science\u201d is a horror staple, and I'm not going to shy away from that terminology just because it's not politically correct these days.)<br /> <br /> Likewise, I have no objection to dealing with modified people and creations as well as the guys who do the science and engineering. The modified people would be more like tier 3 hunters d their Endowments than like deviants by default, and the creations would be more like the Imbued from <b>World of Darkness: Antagonists</b> than Prometheans. It's all Mad Science, after all. It's just that I haven't gotten that far yet. <br /> <br /> I was already thinking that Innovations might take three forms: Mods, Feats, and Devices. In a nutshell, Mods alter what you <i>are</i> (\u201cTo Be\u201d); Feats alter what you <i>do</i> (\u201cTo Do\u201d), and Devices change what you <i>possess</i> (\u201cTo Have\u201d). Everything I've talked about regarding Innovations prior to this post have actually been about Feats. <br /> <br /> Mods involve a subject (human or animal) who gets altered by an Innovation, who picks up the Mod as a Supernatural Merit; Feats are what the scientists and engineers develop, and what I've been describing as Specialty-like traits that attach to and expand the character's skills; and Devices are Equipment that incorporates Breakthrough technology. There's likely to be a fair amount of overlap between Mods and Devices, with AI and automation Breakthroughs allowing for the possibility of Devices that can think and act on their own to some extent. Feats are at the core of this, as creating a Device or installing a Mod requires the use of a Feat. <br /> <br /> I see Mods and Devices working a bit like <b>Hunter</b> Endowment R&amp;D and <b>Reliquary</b> Relics, but with powers and curses you'd expect from weird science rather than mysticism; and I see Feats working a lot like the Skill Tricks from <b>World of Darkness: Mirrors</b>. Unobtainium is tied to the use of Feats, not Mods or Devices, which means that you need Unobtainium to create Devices or install Mods, but (usually) not to <i>use</i> the Devices and Mods \u2014 which is not to say that Devices and Mods don't need some sort of fuel to work. Mods are usually fueled by Willpower, while Devices are usually fuelled by something like Source (from the Gutter Magic system in <b>Witch Finders</b>).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T13:21:08-07:00","id":956516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=956479#post956479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, my aim is for \u201cminor template\u201d to be a bit of a stretch; these mad scientists/geniuses/whateveryou want to call them are a \u201cminor template\u201d in the same sense that hunters are a minor template. There's a reason why I chose to title this as \u201cMad <i>Science</i>\u201d instead of \u201cMad <i>Scientist</i>\u201d, and why I described the difference between mortal, hunter, and mad scientist solely in terms of how they react to encountering the supernatural. (Also, I'm not going to back off of \u201cMad\u201d; \u201cMad Science\u201d is a horror staple, and I'm not going to shy away from that terminology just because it's not politically correct these days.)<br /> <br /> Likewise, I have no objection to dealing with modified people and creations as well as the guys who do the science and engineering. The modified people would be more like tier 3 hunters d their Endowments than like deviants by default, and the creations would be more like the Imbued from <b>World of Darkness: Antagonists</b> than Prometheans. It's all Mad Science, after all. It's just that I haven't gotten that far yet.<br /> <br /> I was already thinking that Innovations might take three forms: Mods, Feats, and Devices. In a nutshell, Mods alter what you <i>are</i> (\u201cTo Be\u201d); Feats alter what you <i>do</i> (\u201cTo Do\u201d), and Devices change what you <i>possess</i> (\u201cTo Have\u201d). Everything I've talked about regarding Innovations prior to this post have actually been about Feats.<br /> <br /> Mods involve a subject (human or animal) who gets altered by an Innovation, who picks up the Mod as a Supernatural Merit; Feats are what the scientists and engineers develop, and what I've been describing as Specialty-like traits that attach to and expand the character's skills; and Devices are Equipment that incorporates Breakthrough technology. There's likely to be a fair amount of overlap between Mods and Devices, with AI and automation Breakthroughs allowing for the possibility of Devices that can think and act on their own to some extent. Feats are at the core of this, as creating a Device or installing a Mod requires the use of a Feat.<br /> <br /> I see Mods and Devices working a bit like <b>Hunter</b> Endowment R&amp;D and <b>Reliquary</b> Relics, but with powers and curses you'd expect from weird science rather than mysticism; and I see Feats working a lot like the Skill Tricks from <b>World of Darkness: Mirrors</b>. Unobtainium is tied to the use of Feats, not Mods or Devices, which means that you need Unobtainium to create Devices or install Mods, but (usually) not to <i>use</i> the Devices and Mods \u2014 which is not to say that Devices and Mods don't need some sort of fuel to work. Mods are usually fueled by Willpower, while Devices are usually fuelled by something like Source (from the Gutter Magic system in <b>Witch Finders</b>).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good. And a reasonable division. Can you provide some examples of what you currently envision? I find that helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T18:51:00-07:00","id":956686,"title":"","content":"Before I do that, let me remind everybody that since this is Mad Science, the Mods and Devices should always have some sort of drawback serving as a counterpoint to their benefits; something like a Mod that takes a toll on the host's health, or a Device that pollutes the environment. Without that, this could very easily get into territory that's more suited to the Trinity Continuum, flavor-wise.<br /> <br /> Basically, every Innovation that you introduce via Mad Science should require that most dangerous of questions to be asked and answered: \u201cWhat could go wrong?\u201d This is on the meta-level: the inventor or engineer doesn't have to ask the question*; but the player and/or the Storyteller should. And the Innovation's drawbacks should be chosen in accordance with that answer. <br /> <br /> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:10px\">* though he <i>can</i>, and can try to take steps to safeguard against the answer, which in turn triggers a new round of \u201cwhat can go wrong?\u201d, this time with the safeguard\u2026</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-23-2016, 10:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T19:34:50-07:00","id":956701,"title":"","content":"Also, the closest to a \u201ctemplate\u201d here would be the creations; I'm thinking that they might have something like a Pandoran's Rank that defines just how \u201csmart\u201d they are, with human-like intelligence being up around Rank 4 or so. The inventors aren't a template; they're people who have achieved a Breakthrough. And the enhanced aren't a template either; they're people who have received Mods. <br /> <br /> Heck, the three aren't even mutually exclusive. It may be crazy-stupid to operate on yourself; but inventors are potentially crazy-stupid. There's nothing preventing a sapient creation from pursuing science and eventually achieving a Breakthrough. And what really is the difference between installing a Mod in an enhanced human and upgrading a sapient Device? (Which, in turn, is why there's so much overlap between Mods and Devices; in fact, I may unify the two categories and tag the few things that <i>don't</i> overlap as exceptions, such as \u201cuplift technologies\u201d that introduce or enhance intelligence into something that lacks it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-23-2016, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T20:56:31-07:00","id":956762,"title":"","content":"On the earlier \u201cwhat can go wrong?\u201d point, I'd like to set it up to encourage players to come up with \u201cdouble-edged sword\u201d inventions, where the drawbacks are built around the same statement that the effects are built around, differing only in terms of whether you're looking at the core statement as an optimist or a pessimist. <br /> <br /> For instance, a treatment that isolates the subject's emotions. <i>The Benefit:</i> your emotions are isolated, so attempts to influence you take serious penalties, in dice pool reductions and/or additional Doors. <i>The Drawback:</i> your emotions are isolated, so you have trouble empathizing with others and <i>you</i> take penalties when attempting to influence <i>them</i>. The treatment itself would be a Feat (probably Medicine-based) which installs a Mod in the subject that alters his psychological makeup; and the Unobtainium for the Feat might be some sort of exotic mind-altering chemicals.<br /> <br /> Or instead of \u201cisolates\u201d, try \u201ccontrols\u201d: the benefits and drawbacks are the same, the former because it's harder to influence someone who's in complete control of his emotions and the latter because complete control means no spontaneity and a lack of a sense of genuineness in your social interactions that tends to be off-putting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-24-2016, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T06:21:43-07:00","id":957558,"title":"","content":"I like this idea. I also know you have said multibal times that you aren't intrested in retooling it for other uses, that said.<br /> It's always bothered me that no one has managed to reveal the supernatural in the CoD world, we live in the age of Wikileaks and things going viral yet no kindred has gone into a small town hospital and explained that he is undead and wants to stop living the lie? A system where exploring the supernatural can lead to problems would help explain this a bit. The other point I wish to raise is this doesn't need to be limited to science, understanding leading to impossible abilities is also a thing in fiction.<br /> Ok all done trying to hijack your system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T07:55:01-07:00","id":957622,"title":"","content":"Oh, you're not hijacking the thread at all. After all, \u201ca sufficiently analyzed magic is indistinguishable from science.\u201d Applying scientific investigation to supernatural phenomena leads to what I <i>would</i> call \u201coccult science\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T08:53:52-07:00","id":957643,"title":"","content":"Do you want me to try and create another example based on what's been written so far, as I understand it? To see how each part and process works?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T09:03:58-07:00","id":957650,"title":"","content":"Go for it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T09:36:54-07:00","id":957666,"title":"","content":"Alright, I'm going to outline what I think the process and results might be. Most is going to be empty placeholders, until I have time to fill them in, but it should establish the basic structure. <hr /><br /> <b>Character:</b> Dr. Raymond Harris<br /> <br /> <b>Trigger:</b> One night while walking to his car in the parking garage, Raymond overhears his coworker getting into an argument with someone before spontaneously combusting. Autopsy revealed no accelerant was used - they just burst into flames. How is this even possible?<br /> <br /> <b>Investigation 1:</b> Dr. Harris overhears of an arson case where no accelerant was found. He offers his expertise to the fire chief for free in exchange for sample from the scene.<br /> <b>Clues:</b> One of the tenant's genetic material was found wherever the flames were, almost as if their <i>blood</i> was splashed all over the house to cause the fire.<br /> <b>Investigation 2:</b> Raymond sees a video online of a strange beastial figure who calls out to fire... and flame appears in mid air! Recognizing the location by a street sign, they go to investigate.<br /> <b>Clues: </b>Analyzing the compounds that caught fire, they seem odd... as if their chemical properties were <i>altered</i> then sloppily returned to their previous state.<br /> <b>...<br /> Investigation n:</b> Desperate for more information, Dr. Harris locates Elizabeth White, a convicted murderer/arsonist who claims that her latent pyrokinetic abilities were actually responsible for the deaths of her parents.<br /> <b>Clues: </b>After breaking her out of the mental ward and subjecting her to numerous tests and MRIs as she used her abilities, Dr. Raymond believes he's finally found out the missing medium and mechanism behind induced combustion at a distance.<br /> <br /> <b>Breakthrough:</b> Induced Combustion<br /> <b>Unobtainium:</b> Neural tissue from something capable of generating remote spontaneous combustion (Changelings with certain Contracts, Mages with Forces, Psychokinetics (Fire), other strange creatures, etc.).<br /> <b>Fuel:</b> Unstable molecules that have <i>almost</i> been induced to combust. Attempts to &quot;supernaturally&quot; set objects on fire (including the following Innovations) that fail, produce 1 Fuel per 3 Sizes, but must be harvested within the same scene.<br /> <b>Innovations:</b> Alter Flammability (Feat), Remote Combuster (Device), Thermal Negater (Device), Tele-thermal Pattern (Mod)<br /> <br /> <b>Alter Flammability</b> (Feat)<br /> By lathering unstable particles onto an object or creature, their threshold for ignition becomes drastically lower.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Fuel per every 5 Size of the object<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Dexterity + Chemistry - Durability<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant* (1 Turn per 5 Sizes)<br /> <b>Roll Result</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> You've gotten the material on yourself! Any damage or major physical impact or heat increase will cause you to catch fire (and gain the On Fire Tilt).<br /> <b>Failure: </b>Something was wrong with how you applied the molecules, and they've become inert.<br /> <b>Success: </b>The next point of damage or spark that affects the target will cause it to catch fire. It acquires the On Fire Tilt, and must end it as normal.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The target becomes so unstable that it catches fire on its own the very next Turn.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Fire is dangerous. Without adequate protection, <i>you</i> are just at much risk as the target.<br /> <br /> <b>Tele-thermal Pattern</b> (Mod)<br /> Using a series of implanted electrodes to stimulate precise neural activity, another subject can trigger line of sight spontaneous combustion.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Unobtainium for the implant, 1 Fuel per use*.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The recipient gains the Psychokinesis (Fire) Merit at 3 dots, except they use Fuel instead of Willpower, and roll Intelligence + Chemistry.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> The presence of the Unstable Molecules in your system raises you body temperature noticeably. Further more, due to your body already coping with an almost constant fever, you treat Extreme Environments (Heat) as if they were 1 degree worse.<br /> <br /> <b>Remote Combuster</b> (Device)<br /> Using the same blend of exotic radiation, this device can cause even steel to catch fire when activated.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Unobtainium for construction, 1 Fuel per use.<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Firearms + Chemistry - Stamina (or Durability)<br /> <b>Roll Result</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> Backfire! Take your unmodified Chemistry rank in Lethal damage from the heat.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> Particle emissions fail to trigger the proper cascade.<br /> <b>Success:</b> Treat the roll as if using a 0L Weapon that deals damage via fire.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> Additionally, the target catches fire (On Fire Tilt).<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> The heat the device puts out after each use is intense. Every use after the first in a scene inflicts the Extreme Environment (Heat) Tilt upon only the bearer, or increases it by 1, for the remainder of the Scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-26-2016, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T09:51:51-07:00","id":957675,"title":"","content":"Not <i>precisely</i> what I described, but keep going; this might be better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T10:33:26-07:00","id":957698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=957675#post957675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not <i>precisely</i> what I described, but keep going; this might be better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did I deviate?<br /> <br /> Currently: trying to think of a good Breakthrough subject to build everything else off of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T12:46:21-07:00","id":957780,"title":"","content":"You may add some guidelines, like the number of Clues of amount of Inobtanium necessary to mimic a dread power of X level, and how they relate.<br /> For example, the research of a device which allows the user to cloak himself in shadows for a scene may need 20 clues and it\u00b4s use requires of one pinch of ashes of a Mekhet each time .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 08-25-2016, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T15:18:24-07:00","id":957876,"title":"","content":"Is twenty Clues common in the Investigation system? I always got the sense that it tended closer to four to six, considering that the revelation of a clue is the sort of thing to which a scene might be dedicated. Remember, the thing that puts Mad Science out of most peoples' reach isn't the scientist's <i>endurance</i> (i.e., will he be able to collect enough Clues before getting tired of the whole thing?) but rather his <i>tenacity</i> (i.e., each Clue is a warning sign, due to its Mind-Blowing nature, that the scientist may regret investigating further; will he continue to press on despite the warnings?) That shouldn't require an unusually large number of Clues; just Clues that test him.<br /> <br /> That also addresses one of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4714\" data-vbnamecard=\"4714\">Live Bait</a>'s questions: in the Chronicles of Darkness, the existence of the supernatural is an open secret: everyone has had an encounter with it, but nobody talks about it. That's the reason why one of the Breaking Point questions for a regular mortal is &quot;what did you forget?&quot; It's a question about what sort of encounter with the supernatural that you've had and then suppressed, because suffering through an Integrity Breaking Point is not something people want to repeat. That much is already there; I'm just taking advantage of it.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to keep the number reasonably low to preserve the Storyteller's sanity; he has to come up with all of those Clues, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  Corrected typo 03-19-2024, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T15:33:35-07:00","id":957891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=957698#post957698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where did I deviate?<br /> <br /> Currently: trying to think of a good Breakthrough subject to build everything else off of.</div> </div> </div> </div>One place where you deviated was the distinction between Unobtanium and Source. As I envision it, Unobtainium is really, really hard to obtain, and you must go to great lengths to acquire more of it once you've used up your existing stockpile; it's like spending dots of Blood Potency or Arcane Experience; the rarity and sheer amount of effort involved in getting more of it should make the player think twice before committing to the expenditure. Source is much more like a regular fuel stat; it's still weird and quirky and drives the character to do weird and quirky things to refuel; but it's much easier to come by. You use Unobtainium to <i>make</i> Devices and Mods; you use Source to <i>fuel their abilities</i>.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, the line between the two can be blurry. If you're familiar with <b>Promethean 1e</b>'s Athanors, it's a bit like the distinction between Vitriol and Reagent: you &quot;bank&quot; Vitriol in your Athanor, which gives you a self-regenerating pool of Reagent to spend on things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-25-2016, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T20:25:06-07:00","id":958024,"title":"","content":"So, I edited with my example. How well does it match your rules/ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T06:32:07-07:00","id":958190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=958024#post958024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I edited with my example. How well does it match your rules/ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I LOVE IT! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://s2.quickmeme.com/img/ed/ed572f0afdf4402ffa6c51564a8ea91a48d4e2d488cfcbe885f409d4b48e6211.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> Remaining question: how are mad scientist differents from the average mortal, to allow them to research and build up thaumo-tech?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T06:45:27-07:00","id":958196,"title":"","content":"They aren't. That's the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T06:49:59-07:00","id":958199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=958196#post958196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They aren't. That's the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the intuitive logic gaps, taking supernatural elements with modern tech and cobble them up together in impossible ways... Isn't that supposed to be... well, impossible for the average non-template guy even in the World of Darkness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 08-26-2016, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T07:03:52-07:00","id":958207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=958190#post958190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remaining question: how are mad scientist differents from the average mortal, to allow them to research and build up thaumo-tech?</div> </div> </div> </div>The average mortal sees the odd and either turns away, or tries to kill it (Hunters). The Mad Scientist goes &quot;but <i>why</i>, though?&quot; (Alternatively: &quot;FOR SCIENCE!&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T07:06:43-07:00","id":958209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=958199#post958199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the intuitive logic gaps, taking supernatural elements with modern tech and cobble them up together in impossible ways... Isn't that supposed to be... well, impossible for the average non-template guy even in the World of Darkness?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who says? Obviously (at least in a/the GMC), Occult Matrices work to produce output. Supernatural stuff has <i>some</i> underlying mechanisms. A person just has to find it.<br /> <br /> Granted, even knowing how, they might lack certain key mechanisms to do much with it (such as not having Pyros, or being able to draw down Supernal Symbols, etc.), but that doesn't mean everything is beyond understanding or manipulation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T07:54:04-07:00","id":958228,"title":"","content":"I think I've said this before, but it's worth repeating: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> gets it. It's not that mad scientists are allowed to do something that regular scientists are forbidden from doing; it's that mad scientists (as in, students of mad science, not scientists who are mad) choose to go places that regular scientists refuse to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T13:43:53-07:00","id":958391,"title":"","content":"On Fuel: an unanswered question is how much Fuel a given character gets for his Mods, how necessary Fuel is (that is, when is &quot;0&quot; an appropriate cost); and how much Fuel each Gadget gets. <br /> <br /> Note also that another way that Mad Science is drawing inspiration from <b>Hunter</b> is that it's not trying to present a unified metaphysics to explain everything -- heck, that would be directly contrary to its central idea, that there <i>isn't</i> a unified metaphysics, only the illusion of one. That's why I never specify the nature of Unobtainium and Fuel, only their relevant properties. And that's why Mods and Gadgets probably feel a lot like <b>Hunter</b>'s Endowments, with more of a focus on what they do than on how they do it. <br /> <br /> Mind you, <i>within the context of a Breakthrough</i>, you can have a unified metaphysics and answers as to why things work as well as what things do. To that extent, each Breakthrough extends the illusion of a sane universe at the cost of complicating the model one uses to understand it. But each Breakthrough also puts more of a strain on that illusion: in a general sense, every exception you have to account for hurts further efforts to maintain credulity. And what happens when you have multiple Breakthroughs that flat-out <i>contradict</i> each other? <br /> <br /> I'm thinking that the more Breakthroughs a Mad Scientist has achieved, the more of a penalty he suffers on further Breakthrough-related Breaking Points. Mind you, he won't suffer <i>any</i> Breaking Points for the weirdness of phenomena that are covered by those Breakthroughs that he's already achieved; his perspective has already adjusted to account for them (although he's still subject to Breaking Points when bad things happen pertaining to Breakthrough phenomena). But his <i>next</i> Breakthrough? Those Mind-Blowing Clues are more likely to blow his mind -- <i>especially</i> if the new Breakthrough's metaphysics clash with what he's already accepted. Finding evidence that contradictory Breakthroughs are <i>both</i> valid is not good for one's mental health.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T14:32:44-07:00","id":958422,"title":"","content":"Another effect of there not being a unified metaphysics is that Breakthroughs can tap into the metaphysics of other gamelines. I've already indicated this when I suggested that a suitable Breakthrough could allow a Mad Scientist to tap into Pyros; I'm figuring that a Mad Science Breakthrough of &quot;Pyros Alchemy&quot; could replace <b>Promethean 2e</b>'s Alchemist rules, and that the Genitive Act could be one of that Breakthrough's Feats. That is, if you want a Mad Scientist to create a Frankenstein monster a la <b>Promethean</b>, you can do it. And this by no means precludes a Mad Scientist with a Breakthrough unrelated to Pyros from crafting a created being, under different metaphysics; but <i>that</i> created being wouldn't be a Promethean. <br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure that a similar logic will apply to <b>Deviant</b>, once that game is out: that is, applying Mods to a subject runs the risk of bestowing a Breaktrough-appropriate template on said subject. Or perhaps it's possible to choose a Feat centered around <i>deliberately</i> bestowing a template. This would likely have a high Unobtainium cost and/or a serious Drawback, especially if you're bestowing a greater template; and it depends on the metaphysics allowing it. <br /> <br /> For instance, a Mad Scientist who develops a Breakthrough involving sublime symbols that define reality could develop Innovations that tap into <b>Mage</b>'s metaphysics; but (for flavor reasons) they'd probably do so from a techgnostic angle, and the Feats would be akin to individual spells; the Mad Scientist would not become a mage. And although he might choose to research how to bestow the Mage template, such an effort would likely be doomed to failure, as <i>mages</i> haven't been able to figure out how to do so. And even if he <i>did</i> manage it, there's the matter of the mandatory Drawback: you'd probably get something like a False Awakening from <b>Night Horrors: Unbidden</b>. <br /> <br /> Likewise, I could see a Mad Scientist discovering God-Machine Infrastructure and Investigating it, and eventually achieving a Breakthrough that lets him develop Embeds and Exploits. He might even be able to figure out how to use Infrastructure to create a new Angel, probably an Exile; but he probably wouldn't be able to turn a human into a Demon. Probably. (Possibility: after Investigating the phenomenon of Covers, he figures out a way to reverse-engineer the process, and arranges for a <i>human</i> to take on a Cover; and further research allows him to treat a <i>Demonic Form</i> as a possible Cover, leading to a sort of &quot;inverted demon&quot;. Of course, these things might require some Advanced Breakthroughs, and the Unobtainium costs for implementing the Innovations are likely to be prohibitive.)<br /> <br /> Ultimately, nothing is impossible for Mad Science, if the scientist is willing and able to pay the price. In theory, at least; in practice, it's limited to achieved Breakthroughs; and some costs cannot be paid. Put another way, the Storyteller has the tools of Breakthroughs and Unobtainium (as well as the good old-fashioned nerf-bat) to deny a Mad Scientist access to anything he deems excessive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T14:44:22-07:00","id":958430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=958422#post958422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure that a similar logic will apply to <b>Deviant</b>, once that game is out: that is, applying Mods to a subject runs the risk of bestowing a Breaktrough-appropriate template on said subject. Or perhaps it's possible to choose a Feat centered around <i>deliberately</i> bestowing a template. This would likely have a high Unobtainium cost and/or a serious Drawback, especially if you're bestowing a greater template; and it depends on the metaphysics allowing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way Mods are, they probably map closely to Variations (and the inherent Drawbacks map to Scars). Sure, you can load a subject up with cool toys... they'd just be a miserable wreck as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=958422#post958422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For instance, a Mad Scientist who develops a Breakthrough involving sublime symbols that define reality could develop Innovations that tap into <b>Mage</b>'s metaphysics; but (for flavor reasons) they'd probably do so from a techgnostic angle, and the Feats would be akin to individual spells; the Mad Scientist would not become a mage. And although he might choose to research how to bestow the Mage template, such an effort would likely be doomed to failure, as <i>mages</i> haven't been able to figure out how to do so. And even if he <i>did</i> manage it, there's the matter of the mandatory Drawback: you'd probably get something like a False Awakening from <b>Night Horrors: Unbidden</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, they might be able to create effectively a Proximus Dynasty, though... Mods would be the spells from Blessings, and the Curse flows from the Drawbacks...<br /> <br /> (Note to self: Look into Product-Of-Mad-Science Proximus Dynasty. Forces, probably, but what else?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=958422#post958422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise, I could see a Mad Scientist discovering God-Machine Infrastructure and Investigating it, and eventually achieving a Breakthrough that lets him develop Embeds and Exploits. He might even be able to figure out how to use Infrastructure to create a new Angel, probably an Exile; but he probably wouldn't be able to turn a human into a Demon. Probably. (Possibility: after Investigating the phenomenon of Covers, he figures out a way to reverse-engineer the process, and arranges for a <i>human</i> to take on a Cover; and further research allows him to treat a <i>Demonic Form</i> as a possible Cover, leading to a sort of &quot;inverted demon&quot;. Of course, these things might require some Advanced Breakthroughs, and the Unobtainium costs for implementing the Innovations are likely to be prohibitive.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe Imperative generation? Cover assumption seems possible (isn't there a thread about Faceless or something as a Cryptid/Minor Template?). Humans can already use Demonic Forms. Well, the specific abilities, at least. As Gadgets. With the risk of Soul Loss. But they <i>can</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T07:46:15-07:00","id":969896,"title":"","content":"Possibly crazy idea (but where else would that be appropriate), but maybe a Breakthrough instead of modifying one Skill, outright creates a new Skill based on it. Like Remote Combustion becomes a Skill that can be used for certain actions, or Ephemerality becomes a new skill for interacting with Ephemera, etc. Subject to their own Specialties, able to have Interdisciplinary Specialty, but likely not Hobbyist Clique, or Professional Training, since, you know, you just invented it... or did you?<br /> <br /> Basically a Breakthrough means you've discovered a whole other field that needs to be explored (instead of just grouping it under Science, Chemistry, Occult, etc.).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T11:07:09-07:00","id":970049,"title":"","content":"Interesting idea. My inclination would be to have the creation of a new Skill be something that can happen after a Breakthrough has been thoroughly explored \u2014 that is, once you've developed a number of Innovations for the Breakthrough, you can \u201ctrade them in\u201d for a new Breakthrough-specific Skill, called a Field. <br /> <br /> Think of it this way: a Field has tremendous flexibility that comes from having a largely comprehensive grasp of the Breakthrough; it is to the Innovations that the scientist starts out with as a <b>Mage</b> Arcanum is to a collection of spells, letting you devise new Innovations on the fly instead of having to painstakingly develop them one by one. <br /> <br /> In keeping with the \u201cMad\u201d part of Mad Science, this doesn't come without a price. Thing is, I'm not sure what that should be: achieving a Breakthrough already has the \u201cyour perspective is forever altered\u201d thing. My gut instinct is to make this a \u201cdifference of degree\u201d thing, where the altered perspective that was acquired with the Breakthrough intensifies to the point that it now counts as a Persistent Condition, a mental counterpart to the Drawbacks that Mods have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-15-2016, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T11:47:44-07:00","id":970076,"title":"","content":"Maybe each field caps your max Integrity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T11:54:42-07:00","id":970079,"title":"","content":"Ooh; that could work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T23:54:34-08:00","id":1000170,"title":"","content":"\u201cIt's Alive!\u201d<br /> <br /> I was just thinking that if I ever get around to writing this up as a proper document, I should probably start with a section talking about the sorts of phenomena that lead to Breakthroughs. Something like the Unnatural Phenomena and Outsiders from <b>Glimpses of the Unknown</b>: events and creatures that don't fit; Fortean Phenomena. Emphasize that it's the <i>world</i> that's mad before getting bogged down in the efforts to make sense of it and the fruits of those efforts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-25-2018, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T05:24:36-08:00","id":1000713,"title":"","content":"You should totally do this as a document.<br /> <br /> It'll make it easier to keep track of when my biologist friend forces me to do a scientist game with her where we use this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T06:59:02-08:00","id":1000756,"title":"","content":"I don\u00b4t want to talk here about Genius the Transgression (mostly to avoid igniting a flame war), but I like better your approach to the mad scientist figure: they start as normal, respected scientists until the day they take interest in some phenomena of the World of Darkness, developing a pseudoscientific theory to expain it which, while false, it is &quot;good enough&quot; to make its practical applications aka gizmos work.<br /> <br /> This is in fact how the eponymous Victor Frankenstein managed to create his monster: <br /> - He gathered clues from the read of Paracelsus and others alchemists, the analysis of the effects of electricity on matter and the science of chemistry...until he archieved the breakdown of creating life from inanimate matter.<br /> - He required very specific body parts plus a Firestorm (Unobtanium) to make his creature.<br /> - Needless to say, he ended paying a hefty price for his ambitions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T07:39:37-08:00","id":1000779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1000756#post1000756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u00b4t want to talk here about Genius the Transgression (mostly to avoid igniting a flame war), but I like better your approach to the mad scientist figure: they start as normal, respected scientists until the day they take interest in some phenomena of the World of Darkness, developing a pseudoscientific theory to expain it which, while false, it is &quot;good enough&quot; to make its practical applications aka gizmos work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, that just describes Genius.<br /> <br /> I like this because it is lighter weight, and doesn't have a game-line equivalent amount of baggage - it can be inserted anywhere.<br /> <br /> I also just like more material in general. You can never have too many ways to accomplish a goal - and options let you pick which method suits your needs the best for the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T19:38:14-08:00","id":1001152,"title":"","content":"I'll count that as a success, because that was the intent.<br /> <br /> What I need now are examples: examples of Unnatural Phenomena, Outsiders, and possible Breakthroughs they might inspire (with an emphasis on how weird the Chronicles of Darkness can be <i>before</i> the inventors start getting creative); examples of Breakthroughs, possible Clues for achieving them, relevant Unobtainium, Source, and some Innovations they might enable; and examples of Innovations, what they can do, and what unintended Consequences they might have.<br /> <br /> It would also be good to devise a few \u201csignature characters\u201d to give a sense of how broad the possibilities are. It would be nice, for instance, to have a mad painter who can paint a doorway to heaven on the back of a Hawaiian shirt and/or a gateway to hell on a poster (not an original idea, mind you; but my problem is that I lack creativity). The Breakthrough is about how artwork can resonates with the supernatural; the Unobtainium is whatever secret ingredient needs to be incorporated into the paint; the Innovations are tied to artistic expression; the Source (if any) is whatever's needed to activate the paintings; and the Consequences, as always, are \u201cwhat could possibly go wrong?\u201d<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T20:49:00-08:00","id":1001174,"title":"","content":"<b>A Few Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> I have been watching this with great interest. I have a few ideas of my own on how to incorporate Occult Science (great term btw - more evocative than simply &quot;mad&quot; science) into my games. My ideas are largely merit based (the ability to perform Occult Science would essentially be an Endowment or Style). My explanation for what allows this is similar to yours, its not like a mage using his special powers to override reality, but more a person who discovers a fundamental aspect of the universe.<br /> <br /> <b>A few other observations</b><br /> <br /> I like tying the Breakthrough mechanic to the Investigation system. whenever possible, I like hitching new mechanics to pre-existing framework. Its a lot easier to work with something you already know than to try to spin a new system whole - cloth.<br /> <br /> For &quot;Unobtanium&quot;, might I suggest re-purposing the word &quot;Catalyst&quot;? &quot;Unobtanium has a pulpy feel that is a little less at home in the supernatural mystery/horror setting of CofD. <hr /><br /> <b>Re: Possible Breakthroughs</b><br /> Here are few ideas that might work - The idea have in mind for breakthroughs are things that are theoretically possible (or slightly outside of possible), but currently beyond the grasp of Known Science.<br /> <br /> <b>Cybernetics: </b>sophisticated mechanisms that can be grafted to living tissue to restore lost function or grant enhanced capabilities.<br /> <b>Leonization:</b> Reversing or Stalling the Aging process, potentially granting greatly extended lifespans (or possibly immortality).<br /> <b>Matter/Energy Conversion: </b>converting energy into matter and back again, cornerstone of replication and teleportation technologies.<br /> <b>Transferable Consciousness: </b>Converting the mind into format that can be digitally duplicated, saved or transferred to different media.<br /> <b>True VR: </b>Large scale artificially constructed environments that offer full sensory immersion. <hr /><br /> <b>Re:Possible Source</b><br /> I like that this takes a bit from the &quot;Gutter Magic&quot; ruleset from Witchfinder. Here are some ideas of what could be considered Source.<br /> <br /> <b>Calibration: </b>The Innovation requires a very specific set of programming, adjustment or tuning before it can function.This process is frequently lengthy and delicate.<br /> <b>Conjunction: </b>the energy required is generated by specific temporal or astrological events. the Innovation can only be engaged at certain times. <br /> <b>Correspondence:</b> The energy requiredis generated at a particular location.<br /> <b>Esoterica: </b>Reagents harvested and distilled from the physical matter of Cryptids and other exotic organisms. Everything from vampire blood to unicorn horn falls into this category.<br /> <b>Mundane: </b>The Innovation runs on common fuel sources, such as electricity or petroleum. Often requires requires exceptional amounts of mundane fuel to properly function.<br /> <b>Quanta:</b> the most common energy source, drawn from the faint EM field surrounding most individuals. Often a higher degree of energy required to generate even modest effect. (This would be a standard Willpower cost)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T21:51:00-08:00","id":1001185,"title":"","content":"A catalyst is something that enables a chemical reaction <i>without</i> being consumed or changed by the reaction, leaving it ready to be used over and over again. It's pretty much the opposite of what Unobtainium is, where the whole point is that you use it up whenever you make something that's lasting and then have to go out and acquire more of it. It's similar to Source, except that it needs to be a lot harder to come by; that's why I compare it to this like Arcane Experience, dots of Willpower or your power stat, etc.: things that do not regenerate if you spend them, that only come back with effort on your part. Hopefully effort that translates into stories, which is why I'd generally prefer something more interesting and less generic than \u201cspend an Experience\u201d as Unobtainium.<br /> <br /> I personally prefer calling it \u201cUnobtainium\u201d because that term is incredibly descriptive and accurate: it's something hard to obtain. But if another term is needed, maybe something like \u201cRare Source\u201d would work, emphasizing its similarity to Source as well as highlighting its key difference.<br /> <br /> I could maybe see Breakthroughs as Merits; but only for the purpose of character creation. After character creation, the only way to acquire them is through the Investigation system as previously outlined (which doesn't involve the use of Experiences, on the basis that accumulating Clues serves the same purpose that spending some sort of Experience-like resource does, and which in turn is why i ditched the original Insight notion); and even the ones you get during character creation assume that you did the requisite investigation during your backstory. Nobody ever just <i>has</i> Breakthroughs.<br /> <br /> Also, I prefer calling it Mad Science rather than Occult Science because the latter emphasizes only the notion that it goes beyond Known Science, whereas the former focuses on the fact that the more you try to make sense of it, the less sense it's going to make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-10-2016, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T05:13:40-08:00","id":1001316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1001185#post1001185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I prefer calling it Mad Science rather than Occult Science because the latter emphasizes only the notion that it goes beyond Known Science, whereas the former focuses on the fact that the more you try to make sense of it, the less sense it's going to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe meet in the middle and call it &quot;Fringe Science&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T05:26:46-08:00","id":1001321,"title":"","content":"How is that a compromise? Fringe Science misses the point every bit as much as Occult Science does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T06:09:39-08:00","id":1001331,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;occult&quot; fits better. Mad scientists are actually dabblers with the same science the God Machine masters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T08:40:26-08:00","id":1001368,"title":"","content":"Sometimes, yes. Other times, what they come up with has nothing to do with the God-Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T14:54:52-08:00","id":1001507,"title":"","content":"Wasn't Weird Science used at some point as a placeholder name?<br /> <br /> I think it fits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T15:46:27-08:00","id":1001527,"title":"","content":"No more than Occult or Fringe. <br /> <br /> I'll grant this much: scientists who are still clinging to the notion that it's possible to make sense of everything are more likely to call it things like Weird, Fringe, Esoteric, or Occult than Mad. <br /> <br /> But Mad Science remains the single most accurate term to describe it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-10-2016, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T15:54:13-08:00","id":1001529,"title":"","content":"Still looking for Fortean Phenomena to use as examples of Esoteric Science Field Research? That kind of storytelling is actually my strong suit, and you have a good thing going here and I'd like to positively contribute to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T16:28:56-08:00","id":1001540,"title":"","content":"Absolutely! There's a reason I want to front-load the Forteana. Thus far, though, the only things I've been able to think of have been to borrow from <b>Glimpses of the Unknown</b>'s Unnatural Phenomena or <b>Promethean</b>'s Firestorms. If you can provide solid material for bizarre phenomena that are potentially worthy of triggering Breaking Points that \u201crattle one's understanding of the world\u201d, go for it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-10-2016, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T17:09:41-08:00","id":1001551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I prefer calling it Mad Science rather than Occult Science because the latter emphasizes only the notion that it goes beyond Known Science, whereas the former focuses on the fact that <b>the more you try to make sense of it, the less sense it's going to make.</b> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like an adept school from UA to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T17:16:12-08:00","id":1001552,"title":"","content":"I'll take that as a compliment; I've always appreciated UA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T18:38:15-08:00","id":1001577,"title":"","content":"*cracks fingers*<br /> <br /> Alright, here's one of the ideas I have on hand. <br /> <br /> <br /> The M\u00f6bius Woods: Discovered originally by a group of national park rangers while looking for missing campers. The M\u00f6bius Woods are a spacial phenomenon where by walking through a specific path through the forest one enters an unexplored section of the forest that doubles back upon itself like a M\u00f6bius Strip. The Stip, once entered, appears at first to be impossible to leave. However, when the forest rangers eventually set up camp for the night and fell asleep (deciding that staying in one place and trying to figure out what's going on was better than blindly trying to escape) they awoke to find themselves and their belongings back in the national park. They would have believed that their experience was just a bad dream or the result of high anxiety from their search, but luckily for the scientific community one of the rangers had recorded one of their attempts to escape the M\u00f6bius Strip and upon viewing it again realized that they had indeed been trapped the previous day. Since that time only one team of scientists led by a field researcher from Null Mysteriis and an agent from Taskforce: VALKYRIE have managed to re-enter the M\u00f6bius Woods, and from their research the scientific community has been able to learn many things about the Stip and the flora and fauna found there. <br /> ~ Properties<br /> 1. The Stip appears to have the same properties as conventional reality, and tests on the air, soil, and plant life all appear to be made of the same elements as their counterparts outside of the Strip. The same cannot be said for the fauna though.<br /> 2. All fauna within the Stip appear to have evolved in a manner in which none have to sleep. All attempts to induce sleep, via drugs and tranquilizers, results in the death of the specimens (once the body falls asleep, all functions cease and cannot restart even when assisted.) <br /> 3. There are no predators within the Strip, all fauna appear to have evolved without any natural predators, and their reproductive cycles seem to have evolved to ensure that the population doesn't balloon out of control.<br /> 4. Currently the only known way to exit the Strip is by falling unconscious. Whether naturally or assisted all test subjects appear to blink out of existence until they are no longer within the Strip. Observations of the subjects reappearing back in the national park say that the same effect happened in reverse. <br /> 5. Prolonged stay within the Strip is extremely hazardous for a human's psyche. The final experiment made before the VALKYRIE agent lost his faculties and started firing upon any flora, fauna, or field researchers present while shouting about their eyes and how they're all the same was an experiment testing the psychological effects in the human mind by exploring the Strip and generally living within it. In hindsight this was probably not the best choice on the team leaders part after researchers began complaining about a growing anxiety they couldn't quite explain the longer they stayed within the Strip, but casualties were to a minimum so this project was declared an overall success. <br /> ~ Conclusion: The M\u00f6bius Woods may have potentially hazardous psychological effects upon humans who stay for too long within the Strip, but the unique flora, fauna, and spacial properties are considered important enough for a second field research team to be sent in the near future.<br /> <br /> [Side note scribbled at the bottom: The missing campers that the park rangers were looking for were never found and presumed dead. No trace of them has been found in the Park or the Strip, but there was evidence hinting that they went down the path that led to the Strip's entrance.]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 11-11-2016, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T17:49:38-08:00","id":1002007,"title":"","content":"Got another one, to help increase the sample size. It's definitely of a larger scope than the previous and draws heavy inspiration from the aesthetic of both the recent Dr. Strange movie and Monte Cook's Invisible Sun game. <br /> <br /> Reflection: Originally discovered by a Cell of Hunters attempting to stop a Coven of Witches from performing some unknown rite in Chicago. The Cell launched their attack just as the rite concluded and witnessed the cornerstone of the rite, a tall ornate mirror, appear to crack and shatter inwards. This revealed the intention of the rite, to open a portal to some other plane of reality. Before the leader of the Coven could step through said portal they were gunned down by the Cell, and the remaining survivors of the Coven were taken into custody by Taskforce: VALKYRIE. The mirror portal remained though, even though it closed upon the Coven leader's death the mirror itself retained it power as a conduit to another plane. Although the mirror remains in VALKYRIE custody as well, a team of scientists have been given permission by the US government to begin examining and experimenting with the portal under strict supervision and armed guard by VALKYRIE. <br /> The following report documents their findings.<br /> ~ Propeties <br /> 1. The conduit, once transformed by the rouge occultists, appears to be a perminent portal to what we are currently calling &quot;Reflection Space.&quot; The portal remains closed until some physical force from our side of the portal smashes into the cracked surface of the closed portal with enough force to break it. Once open, the portal remains that way for exactly 30 seconds before, for reasons yet unclear, the portal closes and the mirrors surface reforms to exactly how it was before it was shattered. <br /> 2. The portal can be opened from the other side, but the force that's required to open the portal is three times as much. Our expedition team had a bit of a panic when they first tried to return, but luckily our VALKYRIE field operative was able to bring enough firepower to bear in order to open it from the other side. That being said, we don't recommend using firearms to open the portal from the Reflection Space side as we suffered a neadless casualty from one of the stray bullets. <br /> 3. Reflection Space isn't naturally environmentally hazardous towards humans. The dimension as been commonly referred to by field researchers as, and I quote, &quot;M. C. Escher's wet dream&quot; but other than strange and often disturbing spacial anomalies it appears to be relatively unhostile towards human life. However...<br /> 4. Reflection Space is inhabited by beings who can be quite hostile towards humans. These beings range from animalistic to intelligent, generally appear to have some sort of routine or function within Reflection Space, appear to be abstract reflections of places and concepts from Conventional Reality, and almost all react negatively when interacting with what they view as &quot;intruders.&quot; Those entities that appeared capable of reason and sympathy for the field researchers simply indicated that they should leave immediately, before the &quot;Knights&quot; arrive to prevent the field researchers from &quot;warping the Realm any further.&quot; Suffice to say, the field leader declared the away mission concluded shortly afterwards.<br /> 5. Some portion of the population of Reflection Space appear to have an interest in escaping from Reflection Space into Conventional Reality. These beings tried ambushing the field research team as they were on route back to the portal. These creatures exhibited supernatural abilities relating to Reflection Space, and more horrifyingly towards adopting the appearance and mannerisms of the field research team. This led to a pitched fire fight, several more casualties on both sides, and the predicament where two identical members of the field research team came back through the portal. Both individuals were apprehended and quarentened, and after about a weeks time the imposter's supernatural mimicry wore off. After that, the intruded rapidly began to expire and perished only three days later. At this time, the government has no future plans to explore Reflection Space. <br /> ~ Conclusion: Due to the beings of Reflection Space being able to mimic humans to a degree that fools most scientific means, Taskforce: VALKYRIE has perminently locked away the conduit to Reflection Space as a matter of national security. However, the potential for scientific discovery involving Reflection Space remains a great temptation amongst the esoteric community. To this day there are still attempts to recreate the process of creating a conduit to Reflection Space, although as to date there have been no successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T23:53:11-08:00","id":1179130,"title":"","content":"So, it's been over a year since this thread was updated. I like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> 's suggestions, save for one thing: there's nothing about what kinds of Breakthroughs these pockets of weirdness might lead to. <br /> <br /> In other news: I'm really, <i>really</i> looking forward to <b>Deviant</b>, as the more I learn about it the more its concepts seem to be kin to the concepts that we've been developing here. If I had to tie Mad Science to a single gameline, <b>Deviant</b> would be it. For instance, the way <b>Deviant</b> attempts to simplify and streamline (e.g., replacing Virtue, Vice, and Integrity with Conviction and Loyalty) is similar to how this project attempts to keep the mechanics focused and lightweight; the notion of Variations incorporating Scars directly mirrors how all Innovations have Drawbacks; the way that <b>Deviant</b>'s Variations are going to go all in on the toolkit approach matches this project's aim to be as open to as broad a range of possible Innovations as possible; and so on. Even the tendency of Mad Science to drive those who study it to madness tends to echo the death spiral that the Remade find themselves in, though the mechanics are quite different. <br /> <br /> If anything's missing from Mad Science (besides specifics), it's probably insufficient emphasis on obsession that drives the scientist to pursue more and more Breakthroughs and Innovations even after she realizes that it's not healthy to do so. In that regard, mad scientists are a bit like the Awakened in that they're addicted to \u201cmysteries\u201d \u2014 or rather, they find it harder and harder <i>not</i> to Investigate weird phenomena the more Breakthroughs they've had. <br /> <br /> Rather than altering the Integrity stat (even to the extent of introducing something akin to <b>Hunter 2e</b>'s Code), I'd rather tie such a mechanic to the inventor's Breakthroughs, much like her immunity to further supernaturally induced Breaking Points comes from what Breakthroughs she has achieved. In fact, the tendency toward obsession is essentially the \u201cDrawback\u201d that comes with that immunity: phenomena that violate a Breakthrough ought to be harder to ignore. <br /> <br /> Basically, I'd like to keep the character traits for a \u201cmad scientist\u201d down to a list of Breakthroughs and their Innovations, plus whatever mental Conditions they've acquired due to their repeated exposure to Breaking Points.<br /> <br /> How about this: uncovering a Mind-blowing Clue counts as satisfying a Vice: in addition to the Breaking Point, you also regain a point of Willpower. Meanwhile, achieving a Breakthrough counts as satisfying a Virtue: you regain all of your Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-25-2018, 03:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T01:16:25-08:00","id":1179134,"title":"","content":"Another breakthrough I just had:<br /> <br /> On the character sheet, Breakthroughs are represented by a section called \u201cMad Sciences\u201d. Each entry on this list is a Skill \u2014 specifically, a variant on the Science Skill that works just like the Science Skill, except that it works for matters covered by the Breakthrough. The basic Science Skill can't be used for Breakthroughs, and the Mad Science Skills can <i>only</i> be used for their respective Breakthroughs. (Exception: Mind-blowing Clues that lead to a Breakthrough can be Uncovered using the standard Science Skill or by the appropriate Mad Science Skill; but in the latter case, they don't count as Mind-blowing.) <br /> <br /> As corollary to this, you cannot achieve a Breakthrough without spending enough Experiences to buy the first dot in the appropriate Mad Science Skill, <i>as well as</i> having Uncovered enough Mind-Blowing Clues to successfully Uncover the Truth about the Breakthrough. Alternately, achieving the Breakthrough lets you use the Mad Science Untrained until you spend enough Experiences for the first dot. Otherwise, Mad Sciences cannot be used Untrained. <br /> <br /> Innovations show up on the character sheet as \u201cMad Specialties\u201d: Crafts Specialties for Devices, and Medicine Specialties for Mods. There might be other kinds as well (e.g., Computer Specialties for Innovative software; possibly Brawling Specialties for Innovative fighting techniques). You cannot take a Mad Specialty without at least one dot in the appropriate Mad Science, as you need to Uncover Clues using that Mad Science in order to \u201cunlock\u201d a given Innovation. Mad Specialties differ from regular ones in that they don't improve your dice pool; they \u201cmerely\u201d let you do something with that Skill that you otherwise wouldn't be able to do.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-25-2018, 04:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T05:20:19-08:00","id":1179158,"title":"","content":"Read the whole thing just now. As some people said, I like how you\u2019re tying things to existing mechanics. <br /> <br /> Let me get this straight. Mad Sciences and Innovations are basically alternate Skills and Specialties? That you can roll to create Devices, implant Modifications, and perform Techniques? And Breakthroughs are a type of Investigation solved by gathering Mind-Blowing Clues?<br /> <br /> The focus on Skills remind me of the Dark Heroes. Except that Mad Scientists have to make an effort to get their cool tricks, and it\u2019s not even free. <br /> <br /> So far my only worry with this is the possibility that Deviant/Promethean/Demon/Mage might end up absorbing the concepts. Which I consider actually good, since that means you\u2019re touching something print-worthy here. <br /> <br /> Oh, and about \u201cmad\u201d... you could emphasize that \u201cmad\u201d here actually means \u201cof marked by uncontrolled emotion,\u201d not \u201cmentally unstable.\u201d Since the determination to push the limits of known reality is, at its heart, a dangerous passion by itself. (This is also my personal justification for explaining Mad Ones in Mage being called mad)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T06:45:08-08:00","id":1179174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1179134#post1179134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another breakthrough I just had:<br /> <br /> On the character sheet, Breakthroughs are represented by a section called \u201cMad Sciences\u201d. Each entry on this list is a Skill \u2014 specifically, a variant on the Science Skill that works just like the Science Skill, except that it works for matters covered by the Breakthrough. The basic Science Skill can't be used for Breakthroughs, and the Mad Science Skills can <i>only</i> be used for their respective Breakthroughs. (Exception: Mind-blowing Clues that lead to a Breakthrough can be Uncovered using the standard Science Skill or by the appropriate Mad Science Skill; but in the latter case, they don't count as Mind-blowing.)</div> </div> </div> </div>So, each of the &quot;Mad Sciences&quot; is its own distinct Skill that the individual in question is pioneering? Or, I suppose, &quot;plagiarizing&quot; if they are learning it from another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1179134#post1179134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As corollary to this, you cannot achieve a Breakthrough without spending enough Experiences to buy the first dot in the appropriate Mad Science Skill, <i>as well as</i> having Uncovered enough Mind-Blowing Clues to successfully Uncover the Truth about the Breakthrough. Alternately, achieving the Breakthrough lets you use the Mad Science Untrained until you spend enough Experiences for the first dot. Otherwise, Mad Sciences cannot be used Untrained.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the MS Skill doesn't <i>exist</i> until you've completed the Breakthrough, and once you do, then you can use it and spend XP on it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1179134#post1179134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Innovations show up on the character sheet as \u201cMad Specialties\u201d: Crafts Specialties for Devices, and Medicine Specialties for Mods. There might be other kinds as well (e.g., Computer Specialties for Innovative software; possibly Brawling Specialties for Innovative fighting techniques). You cannot take a Mad Specialty without at least one dot in the appropriate Mad Science, as you need to Uncover Clues using that Mad Science in order to \u201cunlock\u201d a given Innovation. Mad Specialties differ from regular ones in that they don't improve your dice pool; they \u201cmerely\u201d let you do something with that Skill that you otherwise wouldn't be able to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Brawl (Percussive Waveform Transmission*), which lets you transmit kinetic energy with minimal loss along a vector. Or, &quot;Punch Laser&quot;, in that you can hit things far away as if they were close. Can't do that normally with Brawl, but it <i>is</i> just an extension of Brawl.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T08:13:44-08:00","id":1179204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1179174#post1179174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, each of the \u201cMad Sciences\u201d is its own distinct Skill that the individual in question is pioneering? Or, I suppose, \u201cplagiarizing\u201d if they are learning it from another.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the idea, yes. Although you first need to achieve the Breakthrough through your own work before you can learn the Mad Science from another. That said, he can guide you through the Investigation process.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1179174#post1179174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the MS Skill doesn't <i>exist</i> until you've completed the Breakthrough, and once you do, then you can use it and spend XP on it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if I'd go so far as to say that it doesn't <i>exist</i> before the Breakthrough; but it certainly isn't accessible until then. And yes, once you've achieved the Breakthrough, you get to use it and buy dots in it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1179174#post1179174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like Brawl (Percussive Waveform Transmission*), which lets you transmit kinetic energy with minimal loss along a vector. Or, &amp;quot;Punch Laser&amp;quot;, in that you can hit things far away as if they were close. Can't do that normally with Brawl, but it <i>is</i> just an extension of Brawl.</div> </div> </div> </div>Essentially, yes. These are the Techniques that I talked about earlier in the thread: ways of using existing Skills that would be impossible if not for the Breakthrough. To be honest, I'm a little leery of including them; I've debated saying that Mad Specialties need to be about making or changing something, as with Crafts and Medicine; at least then the talk about needing Unobtainium to set things up makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T08:44:21-08:00","id":1179215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1179158#post1179158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Read the whole thing just now. As some people said, I like how you\u2019re tying things to existing mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's not entirely my own doing; <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> definitely helped it along by suggesting that it could be tied to the new Investigation mechanics. (BTW, don't forget that you can use Science to Investigate.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1179158#post1179158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me get this straight. Mad Sciences and Innovations are basically alternate Skills and Specialties? That you can roll to create Devices, implant Modifications, and perform Techniques? And Breakthroughs are a type of Investigation solved by gathering Mind-Blowing Clues?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's it in a nutshell. Note that in order for Clues to be Mind-Blowing, the subject matter under investigation needs to be potentially mind-blowing; thus, Forteana: the things mad scientists investigate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1179158#post1179158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The focus on Skills remind me of the Dark Heroes. Except that Mad Scientists have to make an effort to get their cool tricks, and it\u2019s not even free.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark Heroes are designed to be a supernatural template; these guys technically don't even qualify as a \u201cmicrotemplate\u201d, as there aren't any Merits involved \u2014 though the Mad Sciences and Specialties fulfill an equivalent role. Basically, these guys are supposed to be on par with mortals with a Supernatural Merit or two; like hunters or Deviants. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1179158#post1179158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far my only worry with this is the possibility that Deviant/Promethean/Demon/Mage might end up absorbing the concepts. Which I consider actually good, since that means you\u2019re touching something print-worthy here.</div> </div> </div> </div> The fact that you named four different games competing to absorb these concepts heartens me. <br /> <br /> Speaking of Mage, you could do worse than to raid <b>Intruders: Encounters with the Abyss</b> for Forteana ideas. The main difference is that Mage pictures the Abyss as something that the game's protagonists let into the world, whereas the Forteana that Mad Science is based on are already here.<br /> <br /> As well, Promethean's Firestorms also provide good inspiration for Forteana. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1179158#post1179158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and about \u201cmad\u201d... you could emphasize that \u201cmad\u201d here actually means \u201cof marked by uncontrolled emotion,\u201d not \u201cmentally unstable.\u201d Since the determination to push the limits of known reality is, at its heart, a dangerous passion by itself. (This is also my personal justification for explaining Mad Ones in Mage being called mad)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well\u2026 first and foremost, remember that it's the <i>Science</i> that's mad; it ultimately doesn't make sense. But yeah; I could definitely see pointing out that this ultimately isn't about becoming mentally unstable so much as it's about the passion to push the limits \u2014 and the price one pays in doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-25-2018, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T09:55:51-08:00","id":1179237,"title":"","content":"OK; I've updated the first post to reflect my current thoughts on the subject. Are there any significant matters that you think ought to be addressed right up front but aren't?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T10:03:00-08:00","id":1179239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1179204#post1179204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the idea, yes. Although you first need to achieve the Breakthrough through your own work before you can learn the Mad Science from another. That said, he can guide you through the Investigation process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1179204#post1179204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if I'd go so far as to say that it doesn't <i>exist</i> before the Breakthrough; but it certainly isn't accessible until then. And yes, once you've achieved the Breakthrough, you get to use it and buy dots in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I meant not exist as in mechanically, on the character sheet. Joe the Plumber can't buy Blood Potency or Memory, because as far as his sheet is concerned &quot;what are those?&quot;. Can't add to what isn't there.<br /> <br /> Until the Breakthrough, the &quot;Dimensional Phasing&quot; Skill isn't there to add dots or Specialties <i>to</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1179204#post1179204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essentially, yes. These are the Techniques that I talked about earlier in the thread: ways of using existing Skills that would be impossible if not for the Breakthrough. To be honest, I'm a little leery of including them; I've debated saying that Mad Specialties need to be about making or changing something, as with Crafts and Medicine; at least then the talk about needing Unobtainium to set things up makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd suspect you'd still need to do <i>something</i> to you (or wear something) to knee someone from across the room. That then, is where the Unobtainium is used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T10:17:15-08:00","id":1179244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1179239#post1179239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I meant not exist as in mechanically, on the character sheet. Joe the Plumber can't buy Blood Potency or Memory, because as far as his sheet is concerned \u201cwhat are those?\u201d. Can't add to what isn't there.<br /> <br /> Until the Breakthrough, the &amp;quot;Dimensional Phasing&amp;quot; Skill isn't there to add dots or Specialties <i>to</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. I envision the Mad Sciences section of the character sheet looking like the Mental Skills section, except that the names are left blank, to be filled in as the scientist achieves Breakthroughs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1179239#post1179239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd suspect you'd still need to do <i>something</i> to you (or wear something) to knee someone from across the room. That then, is where the Unobtainium is used.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then, how is that different from installing a Mod?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T10:46:36-08:00","id":1179252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1179244#post1179244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then, how is that different from installing a Mod?</div> </div> </div> </div>It... isn't? If you are using an existing skill in some way, it logically <i>shouldn't</i> consume some weird resource? Even for Crafts and Medicine, <i>using</i> the Unobtainium would mean you are making a Device or Mod. The knowledge itself shouldn't require consumption of a rare resource, right?<br /> <br /> The Brawl Specialty above would, yes, require a Mod to be used. Maybe <i>not</i> a good example, then. But I'm trying to think of Physical Skills that require the Breakthrough before being attempted. Generally, they are limited by, well, Physics, as opposed to knowledge. <br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Re: The Great Terminology Debate</b><br /> Is there a problem with calling it Fortean Science?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T10:57:05-08:00","id":1183307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1179252#post1179252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It... isn't? If you are using an existing skill in some way, it logically <i>shouldn't</i> consume some weird resource? Even for Crafts and Medicine, <i>using</i> the Unobtainium would mean you are making a Device or Mod. The knowledge itself shouldn't require consumption of a rare resource, right?<br /> <br /> The Brawl Specialty above would, yes, require a Mod to be used. Maybe <i>not</i> a good example, then. But I'm trying to think of Physical Skills that require the Breakthrough before being attempted. Generally, they are limited by, well, Physics, as opposed to knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, part of the point of Mad Science is that it isn't necessarily as limiting as regular physics is. Learning a theory of ki energies and how proper meditative discipline and physical training can allow you to harness those energies to achieve superhuman feats. The Unobtainium might be some sort of drug regimen that helps adjust the way your body channels the ki energies; and the Downside might be that redirecting your life force like this might interfere with normal health and/or cause long-term problems.<br /> <br /> After thinking it over some more, I do think that Techniques should be kept separate from Mods: they're similar in that both change what the subject, personally, can do; but Techniques differ in that they require you to dedicate Experience to acquire them, with all the implications that go with that. In fact, it might be possible to say that the Unobtainium needed for Techniques might be a special kind of Experience like Arcane Experience or Vitriol.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> 