t be possible. The resulting Technique would be the direct result of that training, and only indirectly made possible by the drug.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T09:55:46-08:00","id":1185238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1185225#post1185225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. Bane gets his strength directly from Venom; what I'm discussing here involves using something to enable training that normally wouldn't be possible. The resulting Technique would be the direct result of that training, and only indirectly made possible by the drug.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... &quot;mystic martial arts&quot; could simply be a particularly common and old field (or group of fields) in Mad Science? Monks and philosophers delving into the nature of personal energy, and uncovering super-human techniques?<br /> <br /> EDIT: If you've ever played through <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mark_of_the_Ninja\" target=\"_blank\">Mark of the Ninja</a>, the ink from the Flower might be Unobtainium. Various techniques might have been made from that discovery, which tattooing amplifies. Or no?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":".  Thought of an example 02-12-2018, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T10:52:03-08:00","id":1185269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1185238#post1185238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So... \u201cmystic martial arts\u201d could simply be a particularly common and old field (or group of fields) in Mad Science? Monks and philosophers delving into the nature of personal energy, and uncovering super-human techniques?</div> </div> </div> </div>Essentially, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T23:03:35-08:00","id":1187756,"title":"","content":"<i>Delurk</i><br /> <br /> This seems interesting and I really like the concept. And, since I had to wait for mod approval before I could post anyway\u2026I got to work on some ideas. Because Mad Science can never have too many independently-moving body parts and horribly-translated latin.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure if I\u2019ve got all the mechanics correct, yet. I drew heavily upon Vent0\u2019s earlier example to make this. Hope you enjoy.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Neuroapstemics</span></div><br /> <br /> <b>Example Triggers</b><br /> <br /> It is a late night for Dr. Printz when a patient arrives at her ER. The man is heavily injured, with one of his arms suffering from accelerated decay. She is eventually forced to amputate the appendage to prevent the infection from spreading any further. The victim does not make it but, to her surprise, the man\u2019s arm continues trashing until his body dies.<br /> <br /> The car accident crippled William Haney, leaving him without the use of his legs. While browsing a support forum, he reads a story by someone claiming to have regained the use of his legs through an unspecified regimen of electrical stimulation. Moderators quickly delete the post as spam, but William wonders: Could he walk again?<br /> <br /> Not all people come to Mad Science with innocent intentions, and Martin Echidna is among them. A serial killer, he has a penchant for slow murder, slicing of various body parts and watching them bleed. During one particularly gruesome bloodletting, he suddenly feels as though he has cut off not his victim\u2019s fingers but his own. How could this happen?<br /> <br /> <b>Example Investigations</b><br /> <br /> <i>Investigation: </i>It is easy to experiment with the confluence of muscles and electricity even within the home, especially when you have a dead animal to do so.<br /> <i>Clue: </i>Shocks of a particular intensity can cause certain muscles to lock or unlock in the absence of conscious nervous action.<br /> <br /> <i>Investigation:</i> Phantom Limbs are a well-known neurosomatic issue in which a person without limbs feels as though they still had said limb.<br /> <i>Clue: </i>By prodding a patient with proper shocks, it is possible to enhance or weaken the somatic effect.<br /> <br /> <i>Investigation: </i>A woman accused of a public robbery claims in court that she did not do so, but was possessed by something that controlled her body.<br /> <i>Clue: </i>Interviewing the woman, and performing a few tests on her, show lingering changes in her neural activity, almost as if something overrode her body from a distance.<br /> <br /> <i>Investigation: </i>Certain dissociative drugs can cause out-of-body experiences, in which the user believes they are no longer inside their body.<br /> <i>Clue: </i>Investigation shows the possibility of feeling \u2018outside\u2019 ones body but still being able to control it.<br /> <br /> <i>Investigation: </i>You find a video in which a dimly-seen person gestures at a machine, and it starts moving on its own. You decide to investigate.<br /> <i>Clue: </i>Tracking down the machine, you see that it has no ability to detect motion.<br /> <br /> <i>Investigation: </i>A certain local spot is famous for blocking phone transmissions, despite reception being good in the surrounding area.<br /> <i>Clue: </i>Placing a receiver and experimenting, it seems as though the electrical signal here is distorted somehow.<br /> <br /> <i>Investigation: </i>Some animals have much faster reflexes than humans.<br /> <i>Clue: </i>By performing careful measurements on the speed of various animals under moderate electrical stimulation, you find that it is possible to improve such speeds even further.<br /> <br /> <i>Investigation: </i>Electric eels have the ability to conduct great amounts of electricity along their skin.<br /> <i>Clue: </i>By letting various electrical equipment interact with the eel, you note the possibility of controlling equipment from a distance under careful training.<br /> <br /> <i>Investigation: </i>Certain members of the biohacker community implant magnets beneath their skin, using them to gain various sensations not otherwise normal to human. How does this affect them?<br /> <i>Clue: </i>By interviewing people who have undergone the procedure (or doing so yourself), you gain an understanding of what it is like to have senses beyond the human norm.<br /> <br /> <b>Breakthrough</b><br /> <br /> Human neurons are capable of interfacing with far more than just the body. With the proper insight, action at a distance can be quite spooky indeed.<br /> <br /> This Breakthrough Skill\u2019s focus is mostly on the ability of the human nervous system to interact despite the severing or absence of neural links. Alternatively, the human can obtain sensory input in a like manner. This thematically allows for moving your hands even after they have been amputated, controlling a prosthetic as though it was a fully functional limb, and sensing the approach of people by merging your skin sensations with that of the floor.<br /> <br /> Drawbacks are typically based around the fact that the human nervous system is not designed for combining with things other than human flesh. When interfacing, this tends to lead to various sensitivities and weaknesses.<br /> <br /> <b>Example Unobtania</b><br /> <br /> Nervous tissue from any creature capable of moving objects without physical interaction.<br /> <br /> An object that has stored a 3+ points of Aether for at least a year.<br /> <br /> The Ampullae of Lorenzini, typically found in a shark.<br /> <br /> <b>Example Fuels</b><br /> <br /> Electric Charge, used to aid the nervous system in expanding beyond its ordinary reach. The Breakthrough allows the gathering of electric charge in a manner similar to that of a Promethean (Promethean Second Edition, p. 170). However, while the Breakthrough allows for gathering Charge, they are not protected by doing so, taking half damage each turn from the power source (Chronicles of Darkness, p.97).<br /> <br /> A particular drug, which is pricey (Resources 3 for five points of Fuel) and most likely illegal.<br /> <br /> Aether, which must be stored in special containers (Resources 4, but reusable).<br /> <br /> <b>Innovations</b><br /> <br /> <i>Somatosensory Displacement (Feat)</i><br /> By forcing Fuel into an object, the Mad Scientist can use it to greatly expand their own sense of touch, bring<br /> <i>Cost: </i>1 Unobtanium to learn. To use the technique, 1 Fuel if a significant part of the object is conducive to electricity, 2 if it is not.<br /> <i>Dice Pool: </i>Wits + (Higher of Composure and Neuroapstemics)<br /> <i>Roll Result</i><br /> <i>Dramatic Failure:</i> The Mad Scientist accidentally scrambles their own nervous system, taking a -2 penalty to all physical actions for the scene.<br /> <i>Failure: </i>The Scientist fails to expand their senses.<br /> <i>Success: </i>The scientist may expand their sense of touch into all objects in contact with them or another object within a number of yards equal to ten times their successes. This grants a bonus equal to the Mad Scientist\u2019s Neuroapstemics to all rolls to detect things around them. This lasts for one scene.<br /> <i>Exceptional Success:</i> The Mad Scientist\u2019s control over his senses is good enough that they can draw back their Fuel after use.<br /> <i>Drawback: </i>Expanding senses in this manner leaves the scientist vulnerable. Any impact on an object that causes at least one point of structure damage inflicts the Stunned tilt.<br /> <br /> <i>Electric control (Feat)</i><br /> Through the use of Fuel, the Mad Scientist may now control any nearby electronic device of which they are aware.<br /> <i>Cost: </i>1 Unobtanium to learn, 1 Fuel to use<br /> <i>Dice Pool: </i>Intelligence + (Higher of Computer and Neuroapstemics) - distance in yards<br /> <i>Roll Result</i><br /> <i>Dramatic Failure:</i> The Mad Scientist\u2019s power goes out of control, causing the device to short out or function in a manner diametrically opposed to their intent.<br /> <i>Failure: </i>The Mad Scientist fails to control the device.<br /> <i>Success: </i>The Mad Scientist may control a device, allowing them to use its ordinary functions.<br /> <i>Exceptional Success:</i> The Mad Scientist manages to leave a lingering effect on any device they are aware of. Further uses within the next 24 hours do not require Fuel.<br /> <i>Drawback: </i>This Feat channel goes both ways: damaging the Device inflicts a point of lethal damage on the Mad Scientist.<br /> <br /> <i>Neural Scrambler (Device)</i><br /> Combining a burst of Fuel with the Techniques used to touch things at a distance, the Mad Scientist may temporarily scramble their victim\u2019s neural system.<br /> <i>Cost: </i>1 Unobtanium to build, 1 Fuel to use<br /> <i>Dice Pool: </i>Dexterity + (Higher of Firearms and Neuroapstemics)<br /> <i>Roll Result</i><br /> <i>Dramatic Failure:</i> The Device shorts out: repairing it requires an hour of work and a point of Fuel.<br /> <i>Failure: </i>The Mad Scientist fails to hit the target.<br /> <i>Success: </i>The attack inflicts a point of lethal damage and lowers the target\u2019s by the Mad Scientist\u2019s rating in Neuroapstemics for the purpose of both dice Rolls and Defense. The penalty diminishes by 1 per turn, and repeated uses reset the penalty.<br /> <i>Exceptional Success:</i> The attack inflicts the Stunned tilt in addition to its penalty.<br /> <i>Drawback: </i>The electrical charge emitted does a point of bashing damage for each use after the first.<br /> <i>Special: </i>This is a ranged attack roll: It is subject to the ordinary rules governing ranged attacks, and anyone capable of dodging firearms subtracts their defense.<br /> <br /> <i>Advanced Prosthetics (Device)</i><br /> The Mad Scientist is capable of grafting artificial parts onto a human body, letting them fully interface with the prosthetics as though it was a natural part of their body.<br /> <i>Cost: </i>1 Unobtanium to build, 1 Fuel per week of use<br /> <i>Effect: </i>Anyone wearing Advanced Prosthetics may store Fuel in the same manner as the Mad Scientist, up to a limit of the Mad Scientist\u2019s Neuroapstemics. More importantly, the Prosthetics can cure any persistent natural Tilt or Condition, such as Arm Wrack, Leg Wrack, or Blindness.<br /> <i>Drawback: </i>The Device costs significant Fuel to keep using. In addition to its weekly use, each failed dice roll costs a point of Fuel. Should the wearer ever run out, the Prosthetics cease functioning and inflict an appropriate Tilt or Condition. Further, any effect that would cause a persistent matching condition destroys the prosthetics, requiring a replacement.<br /> <br /> <i>Controlled Amputation (Mod)</i><br /> A series of exotic transmitters and loosely attached nerve endings allow a being to control all parts of their body - even if that body is across the city.<br /> <i>Cost: </i>1 Unobtanium to install, 1 Fuel per use<br /> <i>Effect: </i>The modified being may spend a point of Fuel to inflict remove a hand, arm, foot, leg, eye or ear from themselves. This inflicts appropriate tilts (in the case of eyes and ears, only if they are both removed), but the modified can continue using them as though they were still attached, allowing, for example, for spying from a distance by placing an eyeball. They may additionally reattach limbs using Fuel (even if said limbs were not removed by use of this Mod), and doing so heals both the Tilt and all unhealed damage their removal originally cost.<br /> <i>Drawback: </i>The drawback to having such easily-removed limbs is that the modified is not the only one who can do so. Whenever the modified being is subjected to Arm Wrack, Leg Wrack, Blindness or Deafness, the appropriate body part is removed from their body. It can be reattached as normal.<br /> <br /> <i>Enhanced Neuron Performance (Mod)</i><br /> By grafting Unobtanium into a being\u2019s nervous system, the Mad Scientist may improve reflexes and bodily control.<br /> <i>Cost: </i>1 Unobtanium to install, 1 Fuel per use<br /> <i>Effect: </i>The modified being can reflexively substitute the Mad Scientist\u2019s Neuroapstemics for any Physical Skill for a single roll or defensive use.<br /> <i>Drawback: </i>The Fuel increases the modified\u2019s sensitivity to electricity: Electrical currents deal an extra point of bashing damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless","user":"Mirthless","date":". 02-20-2018, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless","name":"Mirthless","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T01:06:11-08:00","id":1187774,"title":"","content":"Welcome to the forums, and thank you for the worked example! <br /> <br /> One critique: your rating in the Mad Science skill doesn't factor into the Innovation's pool; or if it does, it factors in as a cap (i.e., use the <i>lower</i> of, not the <i>higher</i>). <br /> <br /> Where the Mad Science comes into play is in the discovery of the Feat: you don't automatically get knowledge of all (or even any) of a Mad Science's Innovations as soon as you achieve your Breakthrough \u2014 well, maybe the first one. But after that, you need to invent each one separately. The Mad Science skill lets you do that, adding the new Innovation to your character sheet as a special kind of Specialty (Crafts for Devices, Medicine for Mods, a suitable Skill for Feats); but after that, it has done its job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T01:44:17-08:00","id":1187779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1187774#post1187774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Welcome to the forums, and thank you for the worked example!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! It's good to be here, and making the example was a lot of fun.<br /> <br /> (I was briefly on the WW forums, but I signed up like two months before they got shut down and then never migrated over.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One critique: your rating in the Mad Science skill doesn't factor into the Innovation's pool; or if it does, it factors in as a cap (i.e., use the <i>lower</i> of, not the <i>higher</i>). </div> </div> </div>I mostly used the higher, at the time, because of the options it gave: Using the lower of scores seemed like a significant Experience tax on actually using the Feat, while using just the skill would likewise mean a need to diversify in ways that don't always suit a particular concept. I don't actually have all that much experience at homebrewing though, so it's possible (probable, even!) that I'm wrong about that.<br /> <br /> As a general rule, though, do you agree with the other implicit assumption I made? Namely, that effects should typically scale with the particular Mad Science Skill, to incentivize actually buying up points in the skill?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where the Mad Science comes into play is in the discovery of the Feat: you don't automatically get knowledge of all (or even any) of a Mad Science's Innovations as soon as you achieve your Breakthrough \u2014 well, maybe the first one. But after that, you need to invent each one separately. The Mad Science skill lets you do that, adding the new Innovation to your character sheet as a special kind of Specialty (Crafts for Devices, Medicine for Mods, a suitable Skill for Feats); but after that, it has done its job. </div> </div> </div>An observation:<br /> <br /> A specialty costs 1 Experience. It does not normally allow you to do anything new: It makes you better at a subset of something you could already do.<br /> <br /> A one-dot Merit also costs 1 Experience. In many cases, it does not grant a dice bonus to doing something, but - particularly for a supernatural merit - <i>does</i> allow you to use existing skills in new ways.<br /> <br /> So, within the existing terminology of the Chronicles of Darkness, wouldn't it be more accurate to perhaps see the Innovations as a new type of Merit rather than a specialty? Especially since that also provides a native, non-exception-based answer to questions like &quot;If Innovations are specialties, how do they interact with Area of Expertise or Interdisciplinary Specialty?&quot;).<br /> <br /> Again, I have very little experience in homebrewing CoD stuff, so it's quite possible that there's reasoning here that I'm missing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless","name":"Mirthless","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T05:04:25-08:00","id":1187807,"title":"","content":"So, something I quickly hashed together based on what was earlier said in this thread about Mad Science skills and what they let you do. It was clear I had some confusion on the exact way a Mad Science Skill worked, earlier, and I figure that perhaps doing some index and collating work would clarify things for me.<br /> <br /> What I\u2019ve come up with so far, on the effects of Mad Science Skills. I\u2019ve also added stuff that seemed to be considered (underlined) and ideas of my own (in italics) to flesh things out, especially for the later dots in the skill.<br /> <br /> Does this seem about right?<br /> <br /> <b>What do Mad Science Skills Give You?</b><br /> <br /> The first dot in a Mad Science Skill:<ul><li>Allows you to buy Innovations.</li> <li>Allows you to use a particular type of Unobtanium to learn Feats, build Devices or Install Mods associated with the Mad Science Skill.</li> <li>Allows you to use a particular type of Fuel to use Feats, Devices or Mods associated with the Mad Science Skill.</li> <li>Grants immunity to Breaking Points based around the Breakthrough.</li> <li>Unspecified effect around clues that make it harder to refuse them.</li> <li><u>Grants a free Feat at its first dot</u><ul><li>Reasoning: This means that, once breakthrough has been achieved, a Mad Science skill becomes immediately useful to the Mad Scientist without further Experience Expenditure.</li> </ul></li> <li><i>Failures on Mind-Blowing clues or new supernatural phenomena always give the persistent Obsession Condition.</i><ul><li>This would help the Mad Scientist actually, well, obsess over new phenomena to learn and explore.</li> </ul></li> <li><i>Gives a penalty to breaking points from supernatural phenomena outside the breaking point.</i><ul><li>-1 per unique Mad Science Skill?</li> <li>Reasoning: The further the Mad Scientist goes down the rabbit hole, the more trouble they have not going down even <i>further</i>.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <br /> Every dot in a Mad Science Skill:<ul><li> Allows its use as a skill in identifying, answering questions, and uncovering Clues as an equivalent Science skill would.</li> <li><i>Strengthens the Innovations the Mad Scientist possesses.</i><ul><li>Reasoning: Incentivizes expending Experiences on the Mad Science.</li> </ul></li> <li><i>Gives a bonus to dice rolls to use a Mad Science skill</i><ul><li>Reasoning: Avoids XP tax to actually use the Innovations you have if you do not possess the associated skill.</li> </ul></li> <li><i>Gives a bonus on breaking points that come from using your form of Mad Science.</i><ul><li>+1 per level in the Mad Science Skill?</li> <li>Reason: Gives an incentive to use Mad Science over normal science: Dr. Raymond Harris has a reason to <i>use</i> his Induced Combustion on pesky people who investigate his kidnapping, instead of just shooting them. More abstractly: The sort of Breaking Points that a Mad Scientist would normally go through from doing this have effectively been baked into the Breakthrough.</li> </ul></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless","user":"Mirthless","date":".  Adding in new information. 02-20-2018, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless","name":"Mirthless","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T07:39:49-08:00","id":1187836,"title":"","content":"I'll get back to you on the specifics here. But one thing you may have overlooked:<br /> <br /> What can you do with the Science skill? I mean the plain old, ordinary Mental Skill that's on everyone's character sheet. I ask because everything you can do with the Science skill, you can do with a Mad Science skill, but within the context of the Breakthrough. That's why it's a skill and not a Discipline or Gift or Arcanum etc. <br /> <br /> For instance, the Investigation rules normally use the Investigation skill to Uncover Clues; but it specifically says that you can use Science instead if it makes sense to do so (such as what Gabby does on NCIS). Well, Uncovering Clues within the field of your Breakthrough <s>can</s>should be done using its Mad Science skill. Answering questions about the phenomena covered by the skill's expertise uses the skill. Recognizing when such phenomena might be in play uses the skill. And so on. <br /> <br /> In short, don't get so wrapped up with the unique things that a Mad Science skill can do but the Science skill can't that you neglect all of the options that are already built in there by virtue of it being a variant of the Science skill. For one thing, this may help you avoid reinventing the wheel: the brilliance of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>'s use of the Investigation rules with Mad Science was that it made use of existing game systems instead of inventing new ones that do the same sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T07:57:07-08:00","id":1187844,"title":"","content":"Alright. Thank you. That answers my main point of confusion (why I would ever want more than one dot). I\u2019ve updated the list to reflect it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless","name":"Mirthless","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T08:10:28-08:00","id":1187850,"title":"","content":"That should also give some ideas about what sorts of stories to tell with Mad Science: what sorts of stories would you tell that would feature the Science skill? Now take those kinds of stories and twist them to include science that's disquieting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T09:03:33-08:00","id":1187864,"title":"","content":"As for Feats, my initial thought here was inspired by <b>Fate Core</b>'s Stunts, which take three forms: Grant a bonus to a Skill, expand what the Skill covers, or let the skill break a rule that skills normally have to abide by. Specialties do the former; Feats were supposed to do the rest. That said, you're right: Feats are essentially Merits that enhance Skills, and should be treated as such. They should have Prerequisites, including a Mad Science skill and the skill being enhanced; they should have an Effect, as all Merits do; and they should always have a Drawback. They also count as Supernatural Merits due to depending on principles of Mad Science. And, as Merits, they can be Styles if that's appropriate.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Merits, the Mad Science skills count as Science where Merits are concerned. So Professional Training that includes Science as an Asset Skill (academics, engineers, hackers, scientists, etc.) also includes all of the Mad Sciences the character knows as Asset Skills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T14:29:22-08:00","id":1187975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mirthless</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1187807#post1187807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, something I quickly hashed together based on what was earlier said in this thread about Mad Science skills and what they let you do. It was clear I had some confusion on the exact way a Mad Science Skill worked, earlier, and I figure that perhaps doing some index and collating work would clarify things for me.<br /> <br /> What I\u2019ve come up with so far, on the effects of Mad Science Skills. I\u2019ve also added stuff that seemed to be considered (underlined) and ideas of my own (in italics) to flesh things out, especially for the later dots in the skill.<br /> <br /> Does this seem about right?<br /> <br /> <b>What do Mad Science Skills Give You?</b><br /> <br /> The first dot in a Mad Science Skill:<ul><li>Allows you to buy Innovations.</li> <li>Allows you to use a particular type of Unobtanium to learn Feats, build Devices or Install Mods associated with the Mad Science Skill.</li> <li>Allows you to use a particular type of Fuel to use Feats, Devices or Mods associated with the Mad Science Skill.</li> <li>Grants immunity to Breaking Points based around the Breakthrough.</li> <li>Unspecified effect around clues that make it harder to refuse them.</li> <li><u>Grants a free Feat at its first dot</u><ul><li>Reasoning: This means that, once breakthrough has been achieved, a Mad Science skill becomes immediately useful to the Mad Scientist without further Experience Expenditure.</li> </ul></li> <li><i>Failures on Mind-Blowing clues or new supernatural phenomena always give the persistent Obsession Condition.</i><ul><li>This would help the Mad Scientist actually, well, obsess over new phenomena to learn and explore.</li> </ul></li> <li><i>Gives a penalty to breaking points from supernatural phenomena outside the breaking point.</i><ul><li>-1 per unique Mad Science Skill?</li> <li>Reasoning: The further the Mad Scientist goes down the rabbit hole, the more trouble they have not going down even <i>further</i>.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <br /> Every dot in a Mad Science Skill:<ul><li> Allows its use as a skill in identifying, answering questions, and uncovering Clues as an equivalent Science skill would.</li> <li><i>Strengthens the Innovations the Mad Scientist possesses.</i><ul><li>Reasoning: Incentivizes expending Experiences on the Mad Science.</li> </ul></li> <li><i>Gives a bonus to dice rolls to use a Mad Science skill</i><ul><li>Reasoning: Avoids XP tax to actually use the Innovations you have if you do not possess the associated skill.</li> </ul></li> <li><i>Gives a bonus on breaking points that come from using your form of Mad Science.</i><ul><li>+1 per level in the Mad Science Skill?</li> <li>Reason: Gives an incentive to use Mad Science over normal science: Dr. Raymond Harris has a reason to <i>use</i> his Induced Combustion on pesky people who investigate his kidnapping, instead of just shooting them. More abstractly: The sort of Breaking Points that a Mad Scientist would normally go through from doing this have effectively been baked into the Breakthrough.</li> </ul></li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>As I was envisioning it, <i>putting the name of the Mad Science on your character sheet</i>, even with no dots, would be enough to let you research Innovations; use Unobtainium to train Feats, build Devices, or install Mods that you've researched; use Fuel to power Innovations that need Fuel, gain immunity to \u201cwitness supernatural\u201d Breaking Points covered by the Mad Science skill, and use the Mad Science skill like the normal Science skill. Without a dot in it, use of it counts as Untrained and suffers a -3 penalty. OTOH, it doesn't cost any Experiences to add a Mad Science skill to your list; you just need to achieve the Breakthrough. <br /> <br /> Adding a dot to the Mad Science skill is a very good idea, though, as it negates that -3 penalty for using the skill untrained. Seeing as how you need to use said skill to research Innovations, and you need to research Innovations before you can use Unobtainium to Actualize them, the only benefit that works reasonably well without that first dot is the immunity to suitable Breaking Points. Adding that dot isn't <i>required</i>; but if you have the Experiences to do so, you probably should.<br /> <br /> I wasn't considering a free <i>Feat</i> with the first dot; I was thinking about a free <i>Innovation</i> with the Breakthrough, and possibly even enough Unobtainium to actualize one instance of it. (I'm using \u201cactualize an Innovation\u201d as shorthand for \u201clearn or teach a Feat\u201d, \u201cbuild a Device\u201d, and \u201cinstall a Mod\u201d.) The motivation is to let the character do something useful with Mad Science as soon as possible; the rationale is that the process of achieving the Breakthrough involves successfully putting your new theories into practice. That is, you don't get a free Innovation when you achieve the Breakthrough; you achieve the Breakthrough when you successfully assemble the Clues and reveal your first Innovation.<br /> <br /> Those were <i>my</i> thoughts; I'll get back to you on yours soon\u2122. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T14:58:15-08:00","id":1187985,"title":"","content":"I could see saying that you Obsess upon encountering \u201cwitness supernatural\u201d Breaking Points (including Mind-Blowing Clues) <i>after</i> you've achieved your first Breakthrough; until then, you're a regular mortal who has had the (mis)fortune of encountering something disturbingly weird. Once you've achieved that Breakthrough, though, you're in the white rabbit's burrow and on your way to Wonderland; from here on out, everything draws you in deeper.<br /> <br /> That may be sufficient by itself. If it isn't, <i>then</i> levy a -1 penalty to degeneration checks for each Breakthrough you have after the first. But let's not add incentives that aren't needed; they just clutter things up. (Likewise with your suggested incentive for using your Innovations: let's see if there's a need for an incentive before implementing one.)<br /> <br /> I can see factoring your Mad Science skill into the capabilities of its Innovations if you want \u2014 but only at the time you actualize Mods or Gadgets. Feats can have their effectiveness based on your own rating, where \u201cyour\u201d means \u201cwhoever learns it\u201d: teaching such a Feat to someone without any dots in the Mad Science skill won't be particularly impressive; and if they haven't achieved the Breakthrough, the Feat will be a supernatural Breaking Point \u2014 not healthy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T16:54:40-08:00","id":1189312,"title":"","content":"What would you call a Clue that <i>would have been</i> Mind-Blowing before your Breakthrough, but isn't now? Because I'm thinking that these are the equivalent of Unobtainium where Feats are concerned. Something like this:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">After achieving a Breakthrough, Mind-Blowing Clues related to it stop being mind-blowing (they no longer count as Breaking Points) and instead become Insightful: each Insightful Clue that you Uncover earns you a point of Insight, an Experience-like resource not unlike <b>Hunter</b>'s Practical Experience. You can use Insight to acquire new <i>Feats</i>: Merits representing new things that you can do because of your understanding of the Mad Science.<br /> <br /> A Feat always has the following properties: it's a Supernatural Merit; it has at least two prerequisites (a Breakthrough and a Skill that it extends in some way); and it always has a Drawback. <br /> <br /> By far the most common of the Feats, Crafting Feats are used to create or modify people or things with properties derived from the Breakthrough. The skill prerequisite is usually Crafts (for <i>Devices</i>) or Medicine (for <i>Mods</i>), but other possibilities exist. Be creative. The Drawback for Crafting Feats is that you need a suitable <i>Unobtainium</i> in order to use them. <br /> <br /> For other Feats, the Drawback should answer the question \u201cwhat could go wrong?\u201d What unintended consequences might you suffer because of the Feat?<br /> <br /> Feats can <i>only</i> be acquired through Insight;<br /> regular Experiences are not enough.</div>(There might be other ways to use Insight; but this is its primary purpose.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-24-2018, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T12:17:41-08:00","id":1189441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1189312#post1189312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would you call a Clue that <i>would have been</i> Mind-Blowing before your Breakthrough, but isn't now? Because I'm thinking that these are the equivalent of Unobtainium where Feats are concerned. Something like this:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">After achieving a Breakthrough, Mind-Blowing Clues related to it stop being mind-blowing (they no longer count as Breaking Points) and instead become Insightful: each Insightful Clue that you Uncover earns you a point of Insight, an Experience-like resource not unlike <b>Hunter</b>'s Practical Experience. You can use Insight to acquire new <i>Feats</i>: Merits representing new things that you can do because of your understanding of the Mad Science.<br /> <br /> A Feat always has the following properties: it's a Supernatural Merit; it has at least two prerequisites (a Breakthrough and a Skill that it extends in some way); and it always has a Drawback.<br /> <br /> By far the most common of the Feats, Crafting Feats are used to create or modify people or things with properties derived from the Breakthrough. The skill prerequisite is usually Crafts (for <i>Devices</i>) or Medicine (for <i>Mods</i>), but other possibilities exist. Be creative. The Drawback for Crafting Feats is that you need a suitable <i>Unobtainium</i> in order to use them.<br /> <br /> For other Feats, the Drawback should answer the question \u201cwhat could go wrong?\u201d What unintended consequences might you suffer because of the Feat?<br /> <br /> Feats can <i>only</i> be acquired through Insight;<br /> regular Experiences are not enough.</div>(There might be other ways to use Insight; but this is its primary purpose.)</div> </div> </div> </div>So <b>Feat</b> = <b>Merit </b>(just one based on a template and called by a different term for ease of reference with the rest of the system)? Oh, and they require special XP. That should have an impact on &quot;balancing&quot;, since it will be harder to muster the Insight XP required for 5-dots than normal Merits.<br /> <br /> Again I say to thee: Can you list some examples, so we can see what it looks like in execution?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T09:46:51-08:00","id":1189897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1189312#post1189312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would you call a Clue that <i>would have been</i> Mind-Blowing before your Breakthrough, but isn't now? Because I'm thinking that these are the equivalent of Unobtainium where Feats are concerned. Something like this:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">After achieving a Breakthrough, Mind-Blowing Clues related to it stop being mind-blowing (they no longer count as Breaking Points) and instead become Insightful: each Insightful Clue that you Uncover earns you a point of Insight, an Experience-like resource not unlike <b>Hunter</b>'s Practical Experience. You can use Insight to acquire new <i>Feats</i>: Merits representing new things that you can do because of your understanding of the Mad Science.<br /> <br /> A Feat always has the following properties: it's a Supernatural Merit; it has at least two prerequisites (a Breakthrough and a Skill that it extends in some way); and it always has a Drawback.<br /> <br /> By far the most common of the Feats, Crafting Feats are used to create or modify people or things with properties derived from the Breakthrough. The skill prerequisite is usually Crafts (for <i>Devices</i>) or Medicine (for <i>Mods</i>), but other possibilities exist. Be creative. The Drawback for Crafting Feats is that you need a suitable <i>Unobtainium</i> in order to use them.<br /> <br /> For other Feats, the Drawback should answer the question \u201cwhat could go wrong?\u201d What unintended consequences might you suffer because of the Feat?<br /> <br /> Feats can <i>only</i> be acquired through Insight;<br /> regular Experiences are not enough.</div>(There might be other ways to use Insight; but this is its primary purpose.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like those rules, and that, combined with your other clarifications (thanks for those!) help a lot. I'll be trying to hash together a new Mad Science over the next week, if you're interested.<br /> <br /> An observation: Would it perhaps be more clear if, instead of saying that the <i>clue</i> is no longer mind-blowing, instead, Mind-Blowing clues have different <i>effects</i>? Specifically, you now no longer suffer Breaking Points, and gain Experience, from them? After all, the nature of the clue hasn't changed: The nature of the Mad Scientist has.<br /> <br /> It also has the advantage that the standard gameplay type tends to involve playing and investigating as a group - having a Clue still be Mind-Blowing but its effects differ by type would make it easier to parse &quot;discovering this Clue is a breaking point for Johnny but not Suzie&quot;.<br /> <br /> In addition, having Insight being the only way to get Feats seems to limit it, especially if there's a play situation where you can't just keep investigating the same types of phenomenon. It took me something like two hours to think up the ten Clues I wrote for Neuroapstemics, and having to actually <i>play</i> through more than like, ten at most would eventually get boring. Perhaps having it work akin to Arcane Experience and Arcana, where it's <i>a</i><i>n </i>option for gaining Feats but not the <i>only</i> one, might yield better results? I dunno.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless","name":"Mirthless","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T10:30:29-08:00","id":1189920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mirthless</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1189897#post1189897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I like those rules, and that, combined with your other clarifications (thanks for those!) help a lot. I'll be trying to hash together a new Mad Science over the next week, if you're interested.<br /> <br /> An observation: Would it perhaps be more clear if, instead of saying that the <i>clue</i> is no longer mind-blowing, instead, Mind-Blowing clues have different <i>effects</i>? Specifically, you now no longer suffer Breaking Points, and gain Experience, from them? After all, the nature of the clue hasn't changed: The nature of the Mad Scientist has.<br /> <br /> It also has the advantage that the standard gameplay type tends to involve playing and investigating as a group - having a Clue still be Mind-Blowing but its effects differ by type would make it easier to parse &amp;quot;discovering this Clue is a breaking point for Johnny but not Suzie&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> In addition, having Insight being the only way to get Feats seems to limit it, especially if there's a play situation where you can't just keep investigating the same types of phenomenon. It took me something like two hours to think up the ten Clues I wrote for Neuroapstemics, and having to actually <i>play</i> through more than like, ten at most would eventually get boring. Perhaps having it work akin to Arcane Experience and Arcana, where it's <i>a</i><i>n </i>option for gaining Feats but not the <i>only</i> one, might yield better results? I dunno.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe requiring at least 50% of the XP to be Insight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T11:08:41-08:00","id":1189940,"title":"","content":"All I was looking for was something to encourage further investigation of a Mad Science. You're right, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23896\" data-vbnamecard=\"23896\">Mirthless</a>: making Insight mandatory in order to develop Feats is overkill; just having Insight available to offset costs should be enough.<br /> <br /> By the way, I was figuring that you shouldn't need more than three or four Mind-Blowing Clues to Uncover a Breakthrough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-27-2018, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T22:41:56-08:00","id":1190153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1189940#post1189940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I was looking for was something to encourage further investigation of a Mad Science. You're right, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23896\" data-vbnamecard=\"23896\">Mirthless</a>: making Insight mandatory in order to develop Feats is overkill; just having Insight available to offset costs should be enough.<br /> <br /> By the way, I was figuring that you shouldn't need more than three or four Mind-Blowing Clues to Uncover a Breakthrough.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I tend to agree. Three seems about right: It represents a significant investment (and three breaking point rolls means you have a fairly large chance of a losing Integrity, even if the Clues are the <i>only </i>things you suffer breaking points from which, let's be honest, it likely won't be). I just wrote up more Clues than necessary for the same reason I wrote up more Fuel and Unobtanium variations than necessary. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Speaking of which:<br /> <br /> How do you envision a Mad Scientist in the breadth of his or her Mad Science skills? Obviously, they can have more than one, but do you normally see them as getting more than about three?<br /> <br /> Similarly, how do you think Unobtanium/Fuel should be handled for various different Mad Science skills? Should they be kept separate? Should they all be the same? Should they still technically represent different sources that are just abstracted into a single pool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless","name":"Mirthless","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T01:18:41-08:00","id":1190173,"title":"","content":"Unobtainium and Fuel absolutely should be customized for each Mad Science. In theory, there's no upper limit to how many Mad Sciences a given character can achieve; he's always being driven to pursue more. The practical limit is a matter of playability: at what point do the difficulties and sheer logistics of keeping track of it all become too much? I don't really know, and I feel that's something to be determined through playtesting.<br /> <br /> One set of examples that my (lack of) imagination leads me to is using the Mad Science rules in conjunction with existing gamelines: <br /> <br /> \u2022 Instead of the official rules for <b>Promethean's</b>'s Alchemists, treat Pyros Alchemy as a Mad Science. Unobtainium is Vitriol; Fuel is Pyros; the ability to create a particular Distillation is a Feat; and the Distillation itself is a Device. Note that in a <b>Promethean</b> game that uses this option, it's probably the only Mad Science that's likely to show up in the game.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Each type of <b>Hunter</b> Endowment might be a Mad Science, with that game's R&amp;D rules being used to determine what sorts of Innovations you can devise and with each one's Unobtainium being chosen to reflect the nature of that kind of Endowment; Fuel, meanwhile, is probably Willpower. This differs from the game's normal assumptions in that the Mad Scientist doesn't need to be part of a Conspiracy.<br /> <br /> \u2022 A mortal who investigates the God Machine might end up developing a Mad Science that gives him access to <b>Demon</b>'s powers in the form of Devices or Mods. As with the <b>Promethean</b> example above, this would likely be the only Mad Science in a <b>Demon</b> game. <br /> <br /> \u2022 If the upcoming <b>Deviant</b> doesn't provide rules for the guys who create Deviants, the Mad Science rules could easily be pressed into service: Variations would be Mods. In fact, while I developed the main concepts of Mass Science before Deviant was announced, this arrangement strikes me as as close to a perfect match as you're ever going to find.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-28-2018, 05:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T02:00:17-08:00","id":1190180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1189441#post1189441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So <b>Feat</b> = <b>Merit </b>(just one based on a template and called by a different term for ease of reference with the rest of the system)?</div> </div> </div> </div>This, right here, is the reason why I was leery about using Merits to represent Feats. No, it's not \u201cFeat=Merit\u201d; it's \u201cFeat=<i>subset of</i> Merit\u201d. The main purpose of the template for a Feat is to identify those characteristics that Merits, in general, may or may not have but that Feats, in particular, <i>must</i> have. <br /> <br /> Crucially, a Feat must have a Skill as a Prerequisite because a Feat is something that extends what a Skill can do. Look over the existing Merits that have Prerequisite Skills: they all are things that are <i>learned</i>, and their Effects involve letting you do things that are related to the Skill but not normally covered by it. That aspect of it is why I'm calling it a Feat; the rest (the Breakthrough Prerequisite and the mandatory Drawback) are what make it part of Mad Science. <br /> <br /> Indeed, I'd be OK with broadening the terminology so that \u201cFeat\u201d means \u201ca Merit with a Prerequisite Skill\u201d, and \u201cMad Feat\u201d means \u201ca Feat you can only get if you've achieved a Breakthrough\u201d, with the mandatory Drawback and the Supernatural category just being consequences of the nature of Mad Science. There reason I finally settled on calling Feats a type of Merit was that it potentially allows for Style Feats; it was a different take on what a Feat can be than what I originally imagined. And if it can open up one such possibility, it might open up others as well.<br /> <br /> Indeed, there may be other Merits associated with the Mad Science rules: installed Mods, for instance, might also be represented by Merits. They don't <i>have</i> to be, if it makes more sense not to; for instance, if you're using the Mad Science rules as an alternate means of acquiring <b>Hunter</b>'s Endowments or <b>Deviant</b>'s Variations, you'll represent them as Endowments or Variations rather than Merits. (See the <b>Hunter 2e</b> sneak peek about Endowments to understand why I'm drawing a distinction between Endowments and Merits.) Likewise, Merits can be used to represent signature possessions, and thus <i>could</i> be used to represent a Device you've built (see <b>Hunter 1e</b>'s Advanced Armory as an example of Merits as gear) \u2014 but again, you don't <i>have</i> to represent Devices as Merits if you don't want to. <br /> <br /> The point is that Merits can represent a <i>lot</i> of things; but Feats only represent a fairly narrow subset of that: the result of some sort of training.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T04:12:39-08:00","id":1190195,"title":"","content":"Also, we need to be careful to avoid accidentally restricting ourselves. For instance, the talks so far about Innovations being Devices, Mods, and Feats? That doesn't take into consideration the possibility of using Mad Science to create life. In a <b>Promethean</b> game, this could be used to let a character make a Promethean. It could also be used to make robots or zombies \u2014 or, more generally, automatons: things with a semblance of life, but lacking free will. Or you might have a Mad Science that attempts to address the \u201cfree will\u201d thing by creating an automaton that's designed to house a ghost or some other ephemeral entity: a Goetia, for instance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T05:54:19-08:00","id":1190225,"title":"","content":"So, what I meant be &quot;Feat = Merit&quot;, is that they are mechanically tracked like Merits. XP Cost is 1 per dot. They go in the Merits section of the Character Sheet. Mechanically, they represent what Merits do (which, as you pointed out, is dang near anything). Yes, they aren't <i>just</i> Merits - they all have similar prerequisites, and a similar structure. But so do Mage or Vampire or whatever specific merits (the unwritten Prerequisite: [Splat]). I mean to say that Feat = Merit doesn't mean Merit = Feat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1190195#post1190195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, we need to be careful to avoid accidentally restricting ourselves. For instance, the talks so far about Innovations being Devices, Mods, and Feats? That doesn't take into consideration the possibility of using Mad Science to create life. In a <b>Promethean</b> game, this could be used to let a character make a Promethean. It could also be used to make robots or zombies \u2014 or, more generally, automatons: things with a semblance of life, but lacking free will. Or you might have a Mad Science that attempts to address the \u201cfree will\u201d thing by creating an automaton that's designed to house a ghost or some other ephemeral entity: a Goetia, for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still, keeping the <b>Merit</b> model, those <i>could</i> be represented as Retainers, Staff, or Familiars (for comparison purposes). The point at which they become full NPCs, is pretty much the same as if Retainers become full NPCs.<br /> <br /> And hey, due to <b>Sanctity of Merits</b>, when your artificial minion turns on you (as is tradition), you get a refund for the lost Retainer/Staff/etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 02-28-2018, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T22:13:58-07:00","id":1337448,"title":"","content":"Trying out a different approach to the mechanics:<br /> <br /> The business about Mind-blowing Clues and assembling them to achieve a Breakthrough is there same. What's different (and hopefully simpler) is what the Breakthrough gives you. <br /> <br /> Instead of a Mad Science skill, you list subject matter that you gained knowledge of in your character sheet: basically, you have a list of what Breakthroughs you've achieved. They might come in multiple levels representing increased mastery of the Breakthrough, or it might be an all-or-nothing thing; I don't know yet. Either way, mastery of a Breakthrough gives you the ability to use the Hunter R&amp;D rules to produce Endowments based on the Breakthrough. If there are lesser degrees of mastery of a Breakthrough, they produce \u201cflawed Endowments\u201d similar to the Variation-and-Scar dynamic in the upcoming Deviant game (which stands a very good chance of rendering this entire thread moot; it's hitting all the right notes so far). <br /> <br /> The idea here is that the categories of Endowments in Hunter are Breakthroughs that (in Hunter) have been achieved and mastered by a long, grueling effort of whole teams of scientists working together. The Conspiracies then codify their discoveries in a way that can be shared with their members, facilitating R&amp;D within the scope of the Breakthrough by anyone with access to those records. In other words, Hunter R&amp;D gets incorporated into Mad Science, as the most stable example of what you can do with a Breakthrough. And depending on how Deviant turns out, it may also get incorporated into this, as a less stable version of R&amp;D. Mad Science provides a way to achieve Breakthroughs without large research teams and massive budgets, but at a cost to the researcher's mental integrity. <br /> <br /> As an example: our researcher looks into alchemical phenomena and uncovers some Mind-blowing Clues which he then assembles to achieve a Breakthrough. With this Breakthrough, he gains the ability to use R&amp;D rules to create Elixirs. He does this independent of the Ascended Ones, achieving the same results they did on his own at the cost of having been hammered by multiple Mind-blowing Clues in the process. <br /> <br /> This replaces all of my talk about different kinds of Innovations, et al. The (extremely open-ended) rules for what Endowments can and can't do covers most of it, save only the creation or modification of life (which is more of Deviant's purview).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-28T05:28:30-08:00","id":1426453,"title":"","content":"I <i><b><u>REALLY</u></b></i> like this thread and it\u2019s premise! Here\u2019s my own set of contributions;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=957622#post957622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After all, \u201ca sufficiently analyzed magic is indistinguishable from science.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>think</i> what you meant to say was either \u201cAny sufficiently analysed magic is indistinguishable from science!\u201d or \u201cAny sufficiently arcane magic is indistinguishable from technology.\u201d<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=970049#post970049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting idea. My inclination would be to have the creation of a new Skill be something that can happen after a Breakthrough has been thoroughly explored \u2014 that is, once you've developed a number of Innovations for the Breakthrough, you can \u201ctrade them in\u201d for a new Breakthrough-specific Skill, called a Field.</div> </div> </div> </div>One way this could be developed further is that, after \u2018acquiring/unlocking\u2019 a Field, developing further Innovations for the Breakthrough that the Field belongs to increases the capabilities of the Field, both in terms of boosting its effects <i>and</i> increasing the number of dots you can put in it. The reasoning behind this would be that the Mad Scientist has uncovered more information on the principles of a particular Breakthrough, increasing their understanding of it and how they can apply that knowledge in a practical(-ish) manner.<br /> <br /> Oh! Just had an idea; what\u2019s limiting us to just one Field per Breakthrough? Each of the latter could have several of the former, with each Field requiring \u2018knowledge\u2019 of a different set of Innovations within their respective Breakthrough. This would represent the MS piecing together different ways to capitalise on the Breakthrough\u2019s principles. We could also have Fields that require Innovations from multiple different Breakthroughs; demonstrating a Mad Scientist leveraging the combined knowledge they possess to greater, or more exotic, effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=970049#post970049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think of it this way: a Field has tremendous flexibility that comes from having a largely comprehensive grasp of the Breakthrough; it is to the Innovations that the scientist starts out with as a <b>Mage</b> Arcanum is to a collection of spells, letting you devise new Innovations on the fly instead of having to painstakingly develop them one by one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thus allowing a Mad Scientist to advance faster along his line of research/inquiry, since they\u2019d not have to dedicate <i>quite</i> as much time to R&amp;D due to having a sufficient amount of context.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=970049#post970049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In keeping with the \u201cMad\u201d part of Mad Science, this doesn't come without a price. Thing is, I'm not sure what that should be: achieving a Breakthrough already has the \u201cyour perspective is forever altered\u201d thing. My gut instinct is to make this a \u201cdifference of degree\u201d thing, where the altered perspective that was acquired with the Breakthrough intensifies to the point that it now counts as a Persistent Condition, a mental counterpart to the Drawbacks that Mods have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure on it, but one possible way to go about this is that the MS develops some sort of quirk in their behaviour and/or method of logical thinking that makes him come across as something of an oddball or weirdo to those either not familiar them as a person and/or not sufficiently familiar with the requisite Breakthrough(s) and Field(s).<br /> <br /> Also, has anyone thought about what a Mad Scientist who\u2019s a) gone completely off the deep end and/or b) researched every last Breakthrough, puzzled out every last Innovation and (if we go for integrating my Feat ideas in some form) \u2018unlocked\u2019 every last Feat be like?<br /> <br /> Note: I never said they\u2019d be <i>GOOD</i> in terms of quality, just that I was providing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-28T16:26:59-08:00","id":1426505,"title":"","content":"I mean, since this was revitalized (<i>It's ALIVE!!!</i>), each Field could also serve as justification for atypically powerful Equipment via the Build Equipment rules. Sure, I wouldn't let someone build a handgun with a 5 Weapon modifier, +5 to attack rolls, and sets you on fire and/or Stuns normally... but if you have a Plasma Dynamics Field, I might.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-29T05:06:11-08:00","id":1426567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1426505#post1426505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, since this was revitalized (<i>It's ALIVE!!!</i>), each Field could also serve as justification for atypically powerful Equipment via the Build Equipment rules. Sure, I wouldn't let someone build a handgun with a 5 Weapon modifier, +5 to attack rolls, and sets you on fire and/or Stuns normally... but if you have a Plasma Dynamics Field, I might.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, that would make sense! The MS would simply be applying the knowledge and understanding they have to the construction of Equipment. Ergo, said equipment could have properties not normally available to players (so long as they had the necessary Fields, that is).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-29T06:21:29-08:00","id":1426575,"title":"","content":"In general, no. You don't use Science to build equipment; you use Crafts. Fields are more akin to Science than to Crafts.<br /> <br /> That said, we've been using the Investigation rules as a sort of invention system, with Mind-blowing Clues leading to Breakthroughs. I could see using a Field with the Investigation rules to invent a new kind of equipment, which you then use Crafts to build. (The Clues needed for an invention by way of a Field wouldn't be Mind-blowing; you already did that when establishing the Field in the first place.)<br /> <br /> Technically, you could do this Investigation-as-Invention using Science, too; but the resulting Invention would have to conform to regular science and to the current state of technology, which means it would be positively mundane compared to the sorts of inventions that a Field would make possible. For instance, equipment that provides an extra die above and beyond what the standard model provides; useful, but nothing extraordinary.<br /> <br /> That said, I do agree that looking at how the Building Equipment rules interface with Mad Science is a productive endeavor. For instance, how does Availability apply to equipment that's dependent on some sort of Unobtainium to make?<br /> <br /> As well, the Endowment Research and Development rules in the upcoming HtV2e are worth looking at, too. In particular, that system includes (among other things) Advanced Armoury and Thaumatechnology; so to an extent, Hunter R&amp;D is doing something similar and might be worth borrowing from. In particular, I'm thinking of how you can get more powerful Endowments by attaching an activation cost (such as Willpower, bashing damage, or lethal damage; and for Mad Science equipment, I'd add the possibility of an exotic fuel as a possible cost to use) or a backlash (which is phrased in terms of Conditions, and comes in three levels: a consequence that doesn't even rise to the level of a Condition, a consequence that imposes a regular Condition, and a consequence that imposes a Persistent Condition.)<br /> <br /> With Mad Science equipment in particular, the more extraordinary its benefits, the more serious its cost to use and/or its drawback should be.<br /> <br /> Again, this isn't the uplifting Super-Science of the Trinity Continuum; this is a horror game, and Mad Science should be nasty and terrifying. You should always be asking \u201cwhat could go wrong?\u201d, and not rhetorically; because with Mad Science, if anything <i>can</i> go wrong, it <i>will</i>. There will always be unintended and/or unavoidable consequences to using it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  Typos 03-19-2024, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T16:22:08-08:00","id":1426877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1426575#post1426575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, no. You don't use Science to build equipment; you use Crafts. Fields are more akin to Science than to Crafts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, actually:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The type of equipment the character builds determines which dice pool to use. Most physical objects use Wits + Crafts, or Wits + Expression for creative works; organizations may use Presence or Manipulation + Socialize or Streetwise; repositories usually use Intelligence + Academics; and mystical equipment usually uses Wits + Occult. Plans are a slightly different animal, and require a Wits + Composure roll. The Storyteller or player can sug - gest alternatives if appropriate. </div> </div> </div>You don't need to use Crafts. So Fields are valid here too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1426575#post1426575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, we've been using the Investigation rules as a sort of invention system, with Mind-blowing Clues leading to Breakthroughs. I could see using a Field with the Investigation rules to invent a new kind of equipment, which you then use Crafts to build. (The Clues needed for an invention by way of a Field wouldn't be Mind-blowing; you already did that when establishing the Field in the first place.)<br /> <br /> Technically, you could do this Investigation-as-Invention using Science, too; but the resulting Invention would have to conform to regular science and to the current state of technology, which means it would be positively mundane compared to the sorts of inventions that a Field would make possible. For instance, equipment that provides an extra die above and beyond what the standard model provides; useful, but nothing extraordinary.<br /> <br /> That said, I do agree that looking at how the Building Equipment rules interface with Mad Science is a productive endeavor. For instance, how does Availability apply to equipment that's dependent on some sort of Unobtainium to make?<br /> <br /> As well, the Endowment Research and Development rules in the upcoming HtV2e are worth looking at, too. In particular, that system includes (among other things) Advanced Armoury and Thaumatechnology; so to an extent, Hunter R&amp;D is doing something similar and might be worth borrowing from. In particular, I'm thinking of how you can get more powerful Endowments by attaching an activation cost (such as Willpower, bashing damage, or lethal damage; and for Mad Science equipment, I'd add the possibility of an exotic fuel as a possible cost to use) or a backlash (which is phrased in terms of Conditions, and comes in three levels: a consequence that doesn't even rise to the level of a Condition, a consequence that imposes a regular Condition, and a consequence that imposes a Persistent Condition.)<br /> <br /> With Mad Science equipment in particular, the more extraordinary its benefits, the more serious its cost to use and/or its drawback should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can do Investigation-as-Construction if you want to design something <i>big</i> in multiple phases too, yeah. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science?p=1426575#post1426575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, this isn't the uplifting Super-Science of the Trinity Continuum; this is a horror game, and Mad Science should be nasty and terrifying. You should always be asking \u201cwhat could go wrong?\u201d, and not rhetorically; because return Mad Science, is anything <i>can</i> go wrong, it <i>will</i>. There will always be unintended and/or unavoidable consequences to using it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You Ghost-Cannon could, for instance, backfire and dump angry specters everywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}